;; ============================================================================

;; REGISTER ALLOCATION  —  port of Simple's RegAlloc, BuildLRG, IFG, Coalesce, LRG
;; ============================================================================
;;
;; Graph colouring, in ROUNDS. Simple's own summary of the main algorithm, which is the contract:
;;
;;     Repeat until coloured:
;;       Build Live Ranges (LRGs)
;;       - Intersect allowed registers
;;       If hard conflicts (LRGs with no allowed registers)
;;       - Pre-split conflicted LRGs, and repeat
;;       Build Interference Graph (IFG)
;;       - Self conflicts split now
;;       Colour (remove trivial first then any until empty; reverse assign colours)
;;       - If colour fails:
;;       - - Split uncolourable LRGs
;;
;; "Attempt, split, retry" IS the algorithm. An allocator that cannot iterate cannot handle a
;; program that genuinely needs spills. Simple caps its scalar language at 8 rounds and hard-errors
;; past that rather than looping forever. Our moving-GC divergence adds two fixed stack boundaries
;; per live root (Safepoint input and relocation projection); the native relocation regression
;; requires 14 deterministic rounds. We retain the same hard convergence guard with a 16-round
;; budget rather than omitting those GC splits.
;;
;; ## Two economies worth preserving
;;
;; **Liveness and the interference graph are built in ONE pass.** One fewer traversal per round,
;; and there are up to sixteen rounds in the moving-GC target.
;;
;; **A single-register def or use DENIES rather than INTERFERES.** If a live range can only live in
;; RAX, then instead of adding interference edges to every neighbour, it simply removes RAX from
;; each neighbour's allowed set. Simple measures this as a 5x smaller IFG — and the IFG is the only
;; O(n^2) structure in the allocator. Almost every function call does this, as do oddball
;; fixed-register ops like older div/mod/mul.
;;
;; **Simplify order protects biased coloring.** Among currently low-degree ranges, Simple removes
;; broad Split-related ranges first, ordinary broad ranges next, and fixed singleton ranges last;
;; reverse coloring therefore assigns fixed ranges first and leaves Split chains able to follow an
;; already chosen color. Our priority heap preserves that ordering without rescanning the whole
;; trivial set after every removal. At-risk scoring remains Simple's global comparison, while each
;; function's pure scheduled-area term is aggregated once per round.
;;
;; ## What makes this harder than a textbook allocator
;;
;; **Fixed constraints.** Calling conventions pin arguments and results to particular registers, and
;; some machine ops demand a specific one. These are not preferences; a colouring that ignores them
;; is wrong, not merely slow.
;;
;; **Caller/callee save.** A live range crossing a call must be in a callee-save register or be
;; spilled. Simple materialises this: before allocation it adds a `CalleeSave` node to every
;; function's Return for each callee-save register, so the requirement becomes ordinary interference
;; in the same graph rather than a special case in the colourer.
;;
;; **Stack slots continue the register numbering.** Registers are numbered densely from 0, and spill
;; slots continue upward from the last register. So a "register" is either a real register or a
;; spill slot, and SPILLING IS JUST ASSIGNING A HIGHER-NUMBERED REGISTER — not a separate mechanism.
;; See src/codegen/regmask.coil.
;;
;; **Loop Phis get one chance.** A loop Phi that self-conflicts is first split only on its COLD
;; edges; if it self-conflicts again on the next round, its hot def and back edge are split too.
;; Splitting the hot edge first would put a copy in the loop body for a conflict that the cold split
;; would have resolved. During IFG propagation, Simple's `mergeLiveOut` substitutes each live Phi
;; with the arm belonging to that predecessor. Our durable schedule has already visited and killed
;; the Phi definition by then, so we explicitly add the equivalent implicit arm use on every edge.
;; This is what exposes an invariant backedge value overlapping a different entry value.
;;
;; Simple also snapshots and nid-sorts the complete self-conflict set before inserting any splits.
;; Our scalar-key set uses a round-stable stride for the same reason: growing the node arena while
;; handling the first conflict must not make the remaining conflict keys unreachable.
;;
;; **Cloneable endpoints are re-materialized, not copied.** Simple's `makeSplit` clones a cheap
;; machine definition when its output mask overlaps the constrained use. Its `insertBefore` also
;; bypasses an older same-block Split when installing a replacement. Together these rules prevent
;; Split(Box), Split(Split(Box)), ... from reproducing the same conflict in every retry round.
;; Simple's structural `insertBefore` also preserves that clone's position. Our dependency-driven
;; local rescheduler may legally float a pure clone above a later register clobber. When that would
;; invalidate the constrained use again, we retain a real Split: its broad input can live in a
;; spill location across the clobber while its narrow result is materialized on the use side.
;;
;; ## Safepoint liveness carries KINDS, not just liveness  (our addition — Simple has no GC)
;;
;; A slot live at a safepoint is a raw reference, a NaN-boxed word that may CONTAIN a reference, or
;; a scalar — and the collector needs to know which. Liveness that only answers "is it live" cannot
;; produce a stack map for a moving collector, so the kind rides along with the live range from
;; here into src/codegen/gcmeta.coil.
;;
;; ## Post-colouring
;;
;; `postColor` removes no-op spills — a split whose two halves ended up in the same register is a
;; register-to-register move from a register to itself.
;;
(module aot.codegen.regalloc)
(import "coil.alloc" :as alloc)
(import "coil.arraylist" :use *)
(import "coil.hashmap" :use *)
(import "coil.primitive" :as primitive)
(import "coil.os" :as os)
(import "aot.util.panic" :use *)
(import "aot.node.node" :use *)
(import "aot.node.control" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.codegen" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.looptree" :use [looptree-depth-of])
(import "aot.codegen.listsched" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.machine" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.regmask" :use *)
(import "aot.type.type" :use *)

;; Simple's scalar cap is 8. Explicit moving-root stack boundaries require 14 in the native proof.
(const RA-MAX-ROUNDS 16)

;; Live-range kinds, for the stack map. Not in Simple; required by a moving collector.
(const LRG-SCALAR 0)

(const LRG-RAW-REF 1)

(const LRG-BOXED 2)

;; A NaN-boxed word proven not to contain a heap reference still benefits from an addressable spill
;; home across calls, but must not be reported to the collector as a relocatable root.
(const LRG-BOXED-SCALAR 3)

;; Per-block backwards liveness. `defs` stores the representative definition nid for a live LRG;
;; `ids` is the sparse iteration order and retains a key after it is killed, so reinsertion never
;; duplicates work. This replaces one dense LRG-sized allocation and scan for every CFG block.
(defstruct RaLive [(defs (HashMap i64 i64)) (ids (ArrayList i64))])

;; Dense, compilation-owned LRG state. Index zero means "this node has no register value" and is
;; never a union-find member. Lower numbered leaders always win, matching final Simple and making
;; every later failed-set, IFG, and colouring traversal deterministic.
(defstruct RaState
  [(parent (ArrayList i64))
   (masks (ArrayList (Option (ptr RegMask))))
   (kinds (ArrayList i64))
   ;; The fixed entry definition for a whole-function saved register. Final Simple keeps this in
   ;; LRG._machDef for spill-risk scoring; zero means this LRG has no such definition.
   (callee-save-defs (ArrayList i64))
   ;; Final Simple's LRG def/use evidence. Split endpoints drive biased coloring; multiplicity and
   ;; representative machine endpoints drive spill-risk selection in non-trivial cliques.
   (mach-defs (ArrayList i64))
   (mach-uses (ArrayList i64))
   (mach-use-inputs (ArrayList i64))
   (split-defs (ArrayList i64))
   (split-uses (ArrayList i64))
   (multi-defs (ArrayList bool))
   (multi-uses (ArrayList bool))
   (fixed-def-counts (ArrayList i64))
   (fixed-use-counts (ArrayList i64))
   ;; True once a Call/New/JSOP/Safepoint boundary restricted this managed range to the target's
   ;; addressable root homes. Only such ranges may take the managed-root split boundaries; an
   ;; ordinary boxed range with a fixed def and a conflicting fixed use is a plain empty range.
   (root-restricted (ArrayList bool))
   (failed (ArrayList bool))
   (regs (ArrayList i64))
   (liveouts (HashMap i64 i64))  ; (block,lrg) -> representative def nid
   ;; Sparse per-block index into `liveouts`; one record is added on the first successful merge.
   (liveout-heads (ArrayList i64))
   (liveout-lrgs (ArrayList i64))
   (liveout-next (ArrayList i64))
   ;; Reused by the sequential IFG worklist; block revisits do not allocate another sparse set.
   (live-scratch-defs (HashMap i64 i64))
   (live-scratch-ids (ArrayList i64))
   (ifg (HashMap i64 bool))  ; canonical (low,high) interference pair
   ;; Sparse symmetric adjacency. Hash keys deduplicate construction; these lists drive all hot
   ;; degree, simplify, coalesce and coloring walks without scanning the complete LRG id space.
   (adj-heads (ArrayList i64))
   (adj-to (ArrayList i64))
   (adj-next (ArrayList i64))
   (visit-marks (ArrayList i64))
   (visit-generation i64)
   ;; Testable pass counter: coalescing must mutate sparse adjacency, never restart liveness/IFG.
   (ifg-build-count i64)
   (self-conflicts (HashMap i64 bool))  ; (lrg,def nid) pairs for deterministic splitting
   ;; Sparse insertion-order index for self-conflicting definitions. The hash remains the
   ;; membership oracle; this list prevents split selection from scanning the whole node arena.
   (self-conflict-nids (ArrayList i64))
   ;; Focused performance contract: count only actual def-use adjacency inspected while splitting.
   (self-conflict-use-visits i64)
   ;; Hash stride captured before a round's splitter adds nodes. Re-reading arena size while
   ;; splitting would change keys midway through the conflict set and silently skip later defs.
   (self-conflict-base i64)
   (deferred-loop-self (HashMap i64 bool))  ; loop-Phi nid remembered across allocation rounds
   (work (ArrayList i64))
   (on-work (ArrayList bool))
   (degree (ArrayList i64))
   (removed (ArrayList bool))
   (color-stack (ArrayList i64))
   (colour-low-work (ArrayList i64))
   (colour-low-on (ArrayList bool))
   ;; Pure scheduled-area scores are shared by every risky LRG in a function. Build all function
   ;; totals in one CFG pass instead of rescanning the whole CFG for every risk comparison.
   (function-areas (HashMap i64 i64))
   (function-area-ready bool)
   (function-area-block-visits i64)
   (round i64)
   (booted bool)])

(defn ra-state [] (-> (ptr RaState))
  (primitive/alloc-static RaState))

(defn ra-kind-of-node [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [t (n-ty n)]
    (if (ty-memptr? t)
        LRG-RAW-REF
        (if (ty-dyn? t)
            (if (ty-dyn-may-reference? t) LRG-BOXED LRG-BOXED-SCALAR)
            LRG-SCALAR))))

(defn ra-kind-join [(a i64) (b i64)] (-> i64)
  (if (= a b)
      a
      ;; A boxed word needs conservative stack-map treatment if a malformed or transitional LRG
      ;; also contains scalar evidence. Raw references remain precise only when every member agrees.
      (if (or (= a LRG-BOXED) (= b LRG-BOXED))
          LRG-BOXED
          (if (or (= a LRG-RAW-REF) (= b LRG-RAW-REF))
              LRG-RAW-REF
              LRG-BOXED-SCALAR))))

(defn ra-reset-state! [(round i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        state (ra-state)
        (mut id) 1]
    (set! (.parent state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.masks state) (al-new [(Option (ptr RegMask))] a))
    (set! (.kinds state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.callee-save-defs state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.mach-defs state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.mach-uses state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.mach-use-inputs state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.split-defs state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.split-uses state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.multi-defs state) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.multi-uses state) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.fixed-def-counts state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.fixed-use-counts state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.root-restricted state) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.failed state) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.regs state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.liveouts state) (hm-new-scalar [i64 i64] a))
    (set! (.liveout-heads state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.liveout-lrgs state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.liveout-next state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.live-scratch-defs state) (hm-new-scalar [i64 i64] a))
    (set! (.live-scratch-ids state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.ifg state) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a))
    (set! (.adj-heads state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.adj-to state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.adj-next state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.visit-marks state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.visit-generation state) 0)
    (set! (.ifg-build-count state) 0)
    (set! (.self-conflicts state) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a))
    (set! (.self-conflict-nids state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.self-conflict-use-visits state) 0)
    (set! (.self-conflict-base state) (+ (arena-node-count) 1))
    (if (or (= round 0) (not (.booted state)))
        (set! (.deferred-loop-self state) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a))
        0)
    (set! (.work state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.on-work state) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.degree state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.removed state) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.color-stack state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.colour-low-work state) (al-new [i64] a))
    (set! (.colour-low-on state) (al-new [bool] a))
    (set! (.function-areas state) (hm-new-scalar [i64 i64] a))
    (set! (.function-area-ready state) false)
    (set! (.function-area-block-visits state) 0)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.parent state)) 0)
    (push! [(Option (ptr RegMask))] (mut (.masks state)) (None [(ptr RegMask)]))
    (push! [i64] (mut (.kinds state)) LRG-SCALAR)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.callee-save-defs state)) 0)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.mach-defs state)) 0)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.mach-uses state)) 0)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.mach-use-inputs state)) 0)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.split-defs state)) 0)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.split-uses state)) 0)
    (push! [bool] (mut (.multi-defs state)) false)
    (push! [bool] (mut (.multi-uses state)) false)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.fixed-def-counts state)) 0)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.fixed-use-counts state)) 0)
    (push! [bool] (mut (.root-restricted state)) false)
    (push! [bool] (mut (.failed state)) false)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.regs state)) -1)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.adj-heads state)) -1)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.visit-marks state)) 0)
    (push! [bool] (mut (.colour-low-on state)) false)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.degree state)) 0)
    (push! [bool] (mut (.removed state)) false)
    (let [(mut i) 0]
      (loop (if (> (load i) (arena-node-count))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (push! [bool] (mut (.on-work state)) false)
                  (push! [i64] (mut (.liveout-heads state)) -1)
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    (set! (.round state) round)
    (set! (.booted state) true)
    (loop (if (> (load id) (arena-node-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load id))
                  (Some [n] (do (n-set-lrg! n 0) (n-set-reg! n -1)))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                (continue))))
    0))

(defn ra-lrg-count [] (-> i64)
  (if (.booted (ra-state)) (- (len (.parent (ra-state))) 1) 0))

(defn ra-new-lrg! [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (!= (n-lrg n) 0)
      (ra-find! (n-lrg n))
      (let [state (ra-state)
            id (len (.parent state))]
        (push! [i64] (mut (.parent state)) id)
        (push! [(Option (ptr RegMask))] (mut (.masks state)) (None [(ptr RegMask)]))
        (push! [i64] (mut (.kinds state)) (ra-kind-of-node n))
        (push! [i64] (mut (.callee-save-defs state)) 0)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.mach-defs state)) 0)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.mach-uses state)) 0)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.mach-use-inputs state)) 0)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.split-defs state)) 0)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.split-uses state)) 0)
        (push! [bool] (mut (.multi-defs state)) false)
        (push! [bool] (mut (.multi-uses state)) false)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.fixed-def-counts state)) 0)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.fixed-use-counts state)) 0)
        (push! [bool] (mut (.root-restricted state)) false)
        (push! [bool] (mut (.failed state)) false)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.regs state)) -1)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.adj-heads state)) -1)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.visit-marks state)) 0)
        (push! [bool] (mut (.colour-low-on state)) false)
        (push! [i64] (mut (.degree state)) 0)
        (push! [bool] (mut (.removed state)) false)
        (n-set-lrg! n id)
        id)))

(defn ra-find! [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)]
    (if (or (<= id 0) (>= id (len (.parent state))))
        (do (panic-i "ra-find!: invalid live-range id" id) 0)
        (let [(mut leader) id]
          (loop (if (= (get (.parent state) (load leader)) (load leader))
                    (break 0)
                    (do (set! (mut leader) (get (.parent state) (load leader))) (continue))))
          (let [(mut cur) id]
            (loop (if (= (load cur) (load leader))
                      (break 0)
                      (let [next (get (.parent state) (load cur))]
                        (set! (mut (.parent state)) (load cur) (load leader))
                        (set! (mut cur) next)
                        (continue)))))
          (load leader)))))

(defn ra-lrg-of! [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (= (n-lrg n) 0)
      0
      (let [leader (ra-find! (n-lrg n))]
        (n-set-lrg! n leader)
        leader)))

(defn ra-fail! [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [leader (ra-find! id)]
    (set! (mut (.failed (ra-state))) leader true)
    0))

(defn ra-lrg-failed? [(id i64)] (-> bool)
  (get (.failed (ra-state)) (ra-find! id)))

(defn ra-lrg-root-restricted? [(id i64)] (-> bool)
  (get (.root-restricted (ra-state)) (ra-find! id)))

(defn ra-lrg-mask [(id i64)] (-> (Option (ptr RegMask)))
  (get (.masks (ra-state)) (ra-find! id)))

(defn ra-lrg-kind [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (get (.kinds (ra-state)) (ra-find! id)))

(defn ra-lrg-reg [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (get (.regs (ra-state)) (ra-find! id)))

(defn ra-lrg-and-mask! [(id i64) (mask (ptr RegMask))] (-> bool)
  (let [leader (ra-find! id)
        state (ra-state)
        next
          (match (get (.masks state) leader)
            (Some [prior] (mask-and prior mask))
            (None [] mask))]
    (set! (mut (.masks state)) leader (Some next))
    (if (mask-empty? next)
        (do (ra-fail! leader) false)
        true)))

(defn ra-lrg-sub-mask! [(id i64) (deny (ptr RegMask))] (-> bool)
  (let [leader (ra-find! id)
        state (ra-state)]
    (match (get (.masks state) leader)
      (None [] (do (panic-i "ra-lrg-sub-mask!: live range has no allowed mask" leader) false))
      (Some [prior]
            (let [next (mask-sub prior deny)]
              (set! (mut (.masks state)) leader (Some next))
              (if (mask-empty? next)
                  (do (ra-fail! leader) false)
                  true))))))

(defn ra-lrg-deny-reg! [(id i64) (reg i64)] (-> bool)
  (ra-lrg-sub-mask! id (mask-of reg)))

(defn ra-union! [(a i64) (b i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [la (ra-find! a)
        lb (ra-find! b)]
    (if (= la lb)
        la
        (let [leader (if (< la lb) la lb)
              child (if (< la lb) lb la)
              state (ra-state)
              merged-mask
                (match (get (.masks state) leader)
                  (Some [lm]
                        (match (get (.masks state) child)
                          (Some [cm] (Some (mask-and lm cm)))
                          (None [] (Some lm))))
                  (None [] (get (.masks state) child)))]
          (set! (mut (.parent state)) child leader)
          (set! (mut (.masks state)) leader merged-mask)
          (set! (mut (.kinds state))
                leader
                (ra-kind-join (get (.kinds state) leader) (get (.kinds state) child)))
          (if (= (get (.callee-save-defs state) leader) 0)
              (set! (mut (.callee-save-defs state))
                    leader
                    (get (.callee-save-defs state) child))
              0)
          (let [leader-def (get (.mach-defs state) leader)
                child-def (get (.mach-defs state) child)]
            (if (= leader-def 0)
                (set! (mut (.mach-defs state)) leader child-def)
                (if (and (!= child-def 0) (!= leader-def child-def))
                    (set! (mut (.multi-defs state)) leader true)
                    0)))
          (set! (mut (.multi-defs state))
                leader
                (or (get (.multi-defs state) leader) (get (.multi-defs state) child)))
          (let [leader-use (get (.mach-uses state) leader)
                child-use (get (.mach-uses state) child)]
            (if (= leader-use 0)
                (do
                  (set! (mut (.mach-uses state)) leader child-use)
                  (set! (mut (.mach-use-inputs state))
                        leader
                        (get (.mach-use-inputs state) child)))
                (if (and (!= child-use 0) (!= leader-use child-use))
                    (set! (mut (.multi-uses state)) leader true)
                    0)))
          (set! (mut (.multi-uses state))
                leader
                (or (get (.multi-uses state) leader) (get (.multi-uses state) child)))
          (set! (mut (.fixed-def-counts state))
                leader
                (+ (get (.fixed-def-counts state) leader)
                   (get (.fixed-def-counts state) child)))
          (set! (mut (.fixed-use-counts state))
                leader
                (+ (get (.fixed-use-counts state) leader)
                   (get (.fixed-use-counts state) child)))
          (set! (mut (.root-restricted state))
                leader
                (or (get (.root-restricted state) leader) (get (.root-restricted state) child)))
          (let [leader-split (get (.split-defs state) leader)
                child-split (get (.split-defs state) child)]
            (if (or (= leader-split 0)
                    (and (!= child-split 0)
                         (> (n-ltree-depth (match (arena-node child-split)
                                             (Some [n] n)
                                             (None [] (unreachable-node))))
                            (n-ltree-depth (match (arena-node leader-split)
                                             (Some [n] n)
                                             (None [] (unreachable-node)))))))
                (set! (mut (.split-defs state)) leader child-split)
                0))
          (let [leader-split (get (.split-uses state) leader)
                child-split (get (.split-uses state) child)]
            (if (or (= leader-split 0)
                    (and (!= child-split 0)
                         (> (n-ltree-depth (match (arena-node child-split)
                                             (Some [n] n)
                                             (None [] (unreachable-node))))
                            (n-ltree-depth (match (arena-node leader-split)
                                             (Some [n] n)
                                             (None [] (unreachable-node)))))))
                (set! (mut (.split-uses state)) leader child-split)
                0))
          (set! (mut (.failed state))
                leader
                (or (get (.failed state) leader) (get (.failed state) child)))
          (match merged-mask
            (Some [mask] (if (mask-empty? mask) (ra-fail! leader) 0))
            (None [] 0))
          leader))))

(defn ra-assign-to-lrg! [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (id i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [own (ra-lrg-of! n)
        leader (if (= own 0) (do (n-set-lrg! n (ra-find! id)) (ra-find! id)) (ra-union! id own))]
    (n-set-lrg! n leader)
    leader))

(defn ra-deeper-node-id [(old-id i64) (candidate (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (= old-id 0)
      (n-nid candidate)
      (match (arena-node old-id)
        (Some [old]
              (if (> (n-ltree-depth candidate) (n-ltree-depth old))
                  (n-nid candidate)
                  old-id))
        (None [] (n-nid candidate)))))

(defn ra-record-mach-def! [(id i64) (n (dyn NodeOps)) (mask (ptr RegMask))] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        old (get (.mach-defs state) leader)]
    (if (and (!= old 0) (!= old (n-nid n)))
        (set! (mut (.multi-defs state)) leader true)
        0)
    ;; Like Simple, prefer a fixed-register endpoint as the representative.
    (if (or (= old 0) (mask-singleton? mask))
        (set! (mut (.mach-defs state)) leader (n-nid n))
        0)
    (if (mask-singleton? mask)
        (set! (mut (.fixed-def-counts state))
              leader
              (+ (get (.fixed-def-counts state) leader) 1))
        0)
    (if (= (n-op n) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
        (set! (mut (.split-defs state))
              leader
              (ra-deeper-node-id (get (.split-defs state) leader) n))
        0)
    0))

(defn ra-record-mach-use! [(id i64)
                           (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                           (idx i64)
                           (mask (ptr RegMask))] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        old (get (.mach-uses state) leader)]
    (if (and (!= old 0) (!= old (n-nid use_)))
        (set! (mut (.multi-uses state)) leader true)
        0)
    (if (or (= old 0) (mask-singleton? mask))
        (do
          (set! (mut (.mach-uses state)) leader (n-nid use_))
          (set! (mut (.mach-use-inputs state)) leader idx))
        0)
    (if (mask-singleton? mask)
        (set! (mut (.fixed-use-counts state))
              leader
              (+ (get (.fixed-use-counts state) leader) 1))
        0)
    (if (= (n-op use_) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
        (set! (mut (.split-uses state))
              leader
              (ra-deeper-node-id (get (.split-uses state) leader) use_))
        0)
    0))

(defn ra-build-def! [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (mach (dyn MachNode))] (-> i64)
  (match (m-outregmap mach)
    (None [] 0)
    (Some [mask]
          (let [two (m-two-address mach)
                id
                  (if (= two 0)
                      (ra-new-lrg! n)
                      (if (or (< two 1) (>= two (n-nins n)))
                          (do (panic-i "ra-build-def!: invalid two-address input" two) 0)
                          (let [input (n-in! n two)
                                input-id
                                  (if (= (ra-lrg-of! input) 0)
                                      (ra-new-lrg! input)
                                      (ra-lrg-of! input))]
                            (ra-assign-to-lrg! n input-id))))]
            (ra-lrg-and-mask! id mask)
            (ra-record-mach-def! id n mask)
            (if (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-MACH-CALLEE-SAVE)
                (set! (mut (.callee-save-defs (ra-state))) (ra-find! id) (n-nid n))
                0)
            (ra-find! id)))))

(defn ra-build-phi! [(phi (dyn NodeOps)) (mach (dyn MachNode))] (-> i64)
  (match (m-outregmap mach)
    (None [] 0)
    (Some [mask]
          (let [(mut leader) (ra-lrg-of! phi)
                (mut i) 1]
            (if (= (load leader) 0)
                (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins phi))
                          (break 0)
                          (do
                            (match (n-in phi (load i))
                              (Some [arm]
                                    (if (!= (ra-lrg-of! arm) 0)
                                        (do (set! (mut leader) (ra-lrg-of! arm)) (break 0))
                                        0))
                              (None [] 0))
                            (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                            (continue))))
                0)
            (if (= (load leader) 0)
                (set! (mut leader) (ra-new-lrg! phi))
                (set! (mut leader) (ra-assign-to-lrg! phi (load leader))))
            (set! (mut i) 1)
            (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins phi))
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (match (n-in phi (load i))
                          (Some [arm]
                                (let [arm-id
                                        (if (= (ra-lrg-of! arm) 0)
                                            (ra-new-lrg! arm)
                                            (ra-lrg-of! arm))]
                                  (set! (mut leader) (ra-union! (load leader) arm-id))
                                  (n-set-lrg! arm (load leader))))
                          (None [] 0))
                        (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                        (continue))))
            (n-set-lrg! phi (load leader))
            (ra-lrg-and-mask! (load leader) mask)
            (ra-record-mach-def! (load leader) phi mask)
            (load leader)))))

(defn ra-build-node! [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (match (mach-of n)
    (None [] 0)
    (Some [mach]
          (let [op (m-ideal-op mach)]
            (if (or (= op OP-PHI) (= op OP-MEMPHI))
                (ra-build-phi! n mach)
                (do
                  (ra-build-def! n mach)
                  (let [(mut i) 1]
                    (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins n))
                              (break 0)
                              (do
                                (match (n-in n (load i))
                                  (Some [def]
                                        (match (m-regmap mach (load i))
                                          (Some [use-mask]
                                                (let [id
                                                        (if (= (ra-lrg-of! def) 0)
                                                            (ra-new-lrg! def)
                                                            (ra-lrg-of! def))]
                                                  (ra-lrg-and-mask! id use-mask)
                                                  (ra-record-mach-use! id
                                                                       n
                                                                       (load i)
                                                                       use-mask)))
                                          (None [] 0)))
                                  (None [] 0))
                                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                (continue)))))
                  (ra-lrg-of! n)))))))

(defn ra-compress-node-lrgs! [] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut id) 1]
    (loop (if (> (load id) (arena-node-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load id))
                  (Some [n] (if (!= (n-lrg n) 0) (n-set-lrg! n (ra-find! (n-lrg n))) 0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                (continue))))
    0))

(defn ra-success? [] (-> bool)
  (let [(mut id) 1
        (mut success) true]
    (loop (if (or (> (load id) (ra-lrg-count)) (not (load success)))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (and (= (ra-find! (load id)) (load id))
                         (get (.failed (ra-state)) (load id)))
                    (set! (mut success) false)
                    0)
                (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load success)))

(defn ra-first-failed [] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut id) 1
        (mut found) 0]
    (loop (if (or (> (load id) (ra-lrg-count)) (!= (load found) 0))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (and (= (ra-find! (load id)) (load id))
                         (get (.failed (ra-state)) (load id)))
                    (set! (mut found) (load id))
                    0)
                (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load found)))

(defn ra-lrg-sample-nid [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [leader (ra-find! id)
        (mut nid) 1
        (mut found) 0]
    (loop (if (or (> (load nid) (arena-node-count)) (!= (load found) 0))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load nid))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (and (!= (n-lrg n) 0) (= (ra-find! (n-lrg n)) leader))
                            (set! (mut found) (load nid))
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut nid) (+ (load nid) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load found)))

(defn ra-lrg-sample-label [(id i64)] (-> (slice u8))
  (match (arena-node (ra-lrg-sample-nid id))
    (Some [n] (label n))
    (None [] "missing-lrg-sample")))

(defn ra-ifg-base [] (-> i64)
  (+ (ra-lrg-count) 1))

(defn ra-ifg-build-count [] (-> i64)
  (.ifg-build-count (ra-state)))

(defn ra-live-key [(block-id i64) (lrg i64)] (-> i64)
  (+ (* block-id (ra-ifg-base)) lrg))

(defn ra-liveout-nid [(block (dyn NodeOps)) (lrg i64)] (-> i64)
  (if (or (<= lrg 0) (> lrg (ra-lrg-count)))
      (do (panic-i "ra-liveout-nid: LRG out of range" lrg) 0)
      (match (get (.liveouts (ra-state)) (ra-live-key (n-nid block) (ra-find! lrg)))
        (Some [nid] nid)
        (None [] 0))))

(defn ra-ifg-key [(a i64) (b i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [la (ra-find! a)
        lb (ra-find! b)
        lo (if (< la lb) la lb)
        hi (if (< la lb) lb la)]
    (+ (* lo (ra-ifg-base)) hi)))

(defn ra-ifg-interferes? [(a i64) (b i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        la (ra-find! a)
        lb (ra-find! b)
        (mut edge) (get (.adj-heads state) (ra-find! a))
        (mut found) false]
    (if (= la lb)
        false
        (do
          (loop (if (or (< (load edge) 0) (load found))
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (let [other (get (.adj-to state) (load edge))]
                        (if (and (> other 0) (= (ra-find! other) lb))
                            (set! (mut found) true)
                            0))
                      (set! (mut edge) (get (.adj-next state) (load edge)))
                      (continue))))
          (load found)))))

(defn ra-ifg-add-arc! [(from i64) (to i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        idx (len (.adj-to state))]
    (push! [i64] (mut (.adj-to state)) to)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.adj-next state)) (get (.adj-heads state) from))
    (set! (mut (.adj-heads state)) from idx)
    0))

(defn ra-ifg-add! [(a i64) (b i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [la (ra-find! a)
        lb (ra-find! b)]
    (if (= la lb)
        0
        (let [key (ra-ifg-key la lb)]
          (if (hm-contains? (.ifg (ra-state)) key)
              0
              (do
                (set! (mut (.ifg (ra-state))) key true)
                (ra-ifg-add-arc! la lb)
                (ra-ifg-add-arc! lb la)
                0))))))

(defn ra-ifg-merge-adjacency! [(winner i64) (loser i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        (mut edge) (get (.adj-heads state) loser)]
    (loop (if (< (load edge) 0)
              (break 0)
              (let [raw-other (get (.adj-to state) (load edge))
                    other (if (> raw-other 0) (ra-find! raw-other) 0)]
                (if (and (> other 0) (!= other winner))
                    (let [(mut back) (get (.adj-heads state) other)
                          (mut winner-edge) -1
                          (mut loser-edge) -1]
                      (loop (if (< (load back) 0)
                                (break 0)
                                (do
                                  (let [raw (get (.adj-to state) (load back))]
                                    (if (> raw 0)
                                        (let [canonical (ra-find! raw)]
                                          (if (= canonical winner)
                                              (if (= raw loser)
                                                  (set! (mut loser-edge) (load back))
                                                  (set! (mut winner-edge) (load back)))
                                              0))
                                        0))
                                  (set! (mut back) (get (.adj-next state) (load back)))
                                  (continue))))
                      (if (>= (load loser-edge) 0)
                          (if (>= (load winner-edge) 0)
                              (set! (mut (.adj-to state)) (load loser-edge) 0)
                              (set! (mut (.adj-to state)) (load loser-edge) winner))
                          0)
                      (if (not (ra-ifg-interferes? winner other))
                          (ra-ifg-add-arc! winner other)
                          0))
                    0)
                (set! (mut edge) (get (.adj-next state) (load edge)))
                (continue))))
    (set! (mut (.adj-heads state)) loser -1)
    0))

(defn ra-adj-next-generation! [] (-> i64)
  (let [next (+ (.visit-generation (ra-state)) 1)]
    (set! (.visit-generation (ra-state)) next)
    next))

(defn ra-adj-mark-count! [(id i64) (generation i64) (count (mut i64))] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        (mut edge) (get (.adj-heads state) leader)]
    (loop (if (< (load edge) 0)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (let [raw (get (.adj-to state) (load edge))]
                  (if (> raw 0)
                      (let [other (ra-find! raw)]
                        (if (and (!= other leader)
                                 (!= (get (.visit-marks state) other) generation))
                            (do
                              (set! (mut (.visit-marks state)) other generation)
                              (set! count (+ (load count) 1)))
                            0))
                      0))
                (set! (mut edge) (get (.adj-next state) (load edge)))
                (continue))))
    0))

(defn ra-adj-degree [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [generation (ra-adj-next-generation!)
        (mut count) 0]
    (ra-adj-mark-count! id generation (mut count))
    (load count)))

(defn ra-adj-union-degree [(a i64) (b i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        generation (ra-adj-next-generation!)
        la (ra-find! a)
        lb (ra-find! b)
        (mut count) 0]
    ;; The proposed pair itself is not part of the merged neighborhood.
    (set! (mut (.visit-marks state)) la generation)
    (set! (mut (.visit-marks state)) lb generation)
    (ra-adj-mark-count! la generation (mut count))
    (ra-adj-mark-count! lb generation (mut count))
    (load count)))

(defn ra-self-conflict! [(lrg i64) (n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
        key (+ (* leader (.self-conflict-base (ra-state))) (n-nid n))]
    (if (not (hm-contains? (.self-conflicts (ra-state)) key))
        (push! [i64] (mut (.self-conflict-nids (ra-state))) (n-nid n))
        0)
    (set! (mut (.self-conflicts (ra-state))) key true)
    (ra-fail! leader)))

(defn ra-ifg-push-work! [(block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [id (n-nid block)]
    (if (get (.on-work (ra-state)) id)
        0
        (do
          (set! (mut (.on-work (ra-state))) id true)
          (push! [i64] (mut (.work (ra-state))) id)))))

(defn ra-ifg-pop-work! [] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (match (pop! [i64] (mut (.work (ra-state))))
    (None [] (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
    (Some [id]
          (do
            (set! (mut (.on-work (ra-state))) id false)
            (match (arena-node id)
              (Some [n] (Some n))
              (None []
                    (do
                      (panic-i "ra-ifg-pop-work!: missing block" id)
                      (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))))))))

(defn ra-live-scratch! [] (-> RaLive)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        (mut live) (primitive/zeroed RaLive)]
    (hm-clear! [i64 i64] (mut (.live-scratch-defs state)))
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.live-scratch-ids state)))
    (set! (.defs (mut live)) (.live-scratch-defs state))
    (set! (.ids (mut live)) (.live-scratch-ids state))
    (load live)))

(defn ra-live-get [(live (mut RaLive)) (lrg i64)] (-> i64)
  (match (get (.defs live) (ra-find! lrg)) (Some [nid] nid) (None [] 0)))

(defn ra-live-set! [(live (mut RaLive)) (lrg i64) (nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)]
    (if (not (hm-contains? (.defs live) leader))
        (push! [i64] (mut (.ids live)) leader)
        0)
    (set! (mut (.defs live)) leader nid)
    0))

(defn ra-ifg-live-new [(block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> RaLive)
  (let [(mut live) (ra-live-scratch!)
        (mut edge) (get (.liveout-heads (ra-state)) (n-nid block))]
    (loop (if (< (load edge) 0)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (let [lrg (get (.liveout-lrgs (ra-state)) (load edge))]
                  (match (get (.liveouts (ra-state)) (ra-live-key (n-nid block) lrg))
                    (Some [nid] (ra-live-set! (mut live) lrg nid))
                    (None [] (broken "ra-ifg-live-new: sparse live-out index has no definition"))))
                (set! (mut edge) (get (.liveout-next (ra-state)) (load edge)))
                (continue))))
    (load live)))

(defn ra-ifg-check-self! [(lrg i64) (n (dyn NodeOps)) (prior-id i64)] (-> i64)
  (if (and (!= prior-id 0) (!= prior-id (n-nid n)))
      (do
        (match (arena-node prior-id) (Some [prior] (ra-self-conflict! lrg prior)) (None [] 0))
        (ra-self-conflict! lrg n))
      0))

(defn ra-ifg-kills! [(mach (dyn MachNode)) (live (mut RaLive))] (-> i64)
  (do
    ;; Calls and allocations may enter the collector, while an explicit Safepoint describes the
    ;; same relocatable state without emitting a call itself. Every managed value live across any
    ;; of those boundaries receives a stable stack home which the runtime can find and update
    ;; through the frame chain. Scalars retain the ordinary register policy; Barrier is explicitly
    ;; non-collecting and therefore does not pay this constraint.
    (let [op (m-ideal-op mach)]
      (if (or (= op OP-CALL) (= op OP-NEW) (= op OP-JSOP) (= op OP-SAFEPOINT))
          (let [(mut i) 0]
            (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (.ids live)))
                      (break 0)
                      (let [lrg (ra-find! (get (.ids live) (load i)))]
                        (if (and (!= (ra-live-get (mut live) lrg) 0)
                                 (!= (ra-lrg-kind lrg) LRG-SCALAR))
                            (do
                              (set! (mut (.root-restricted (ra-state))) lrg true)
                              (ra-lrg-and-mask! lrg (selected-gc-root-mask))
                              0)
                            0)
                        (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                        (continue)))))
          0))
    (match (m-killmap mach)
      (None [] 0)
      (Some [kills]
            (let [(mut i) 0]
              (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (.ids live)))
                        (break 0)
                        (let [lrg (ra-find! (get (.ids live) (load i)))]
                          (if (!= (ra-live-get (mut live) lrg) 0)
                              (match (ra-lrg-mask lrg)
                                (Some [allowed]
                                      (if (mask-overlap? allowed kills)
                                          (do (ra-lrg-sub-mask! lrg kills) 0)
                                          0))
                                (None [] 0))
                              0)
                          (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                          (continue))))
              0)))))

(defn ra-ifg-node! [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (live (mut RaLive))] (-> i64)
  (match (mach-of n)
    (None [] 0)
    (Some [mach]
          (let [def-lrg (ra-lrg-of! n)]
            (if (!= def-lrg 0)
                (do
                  (ra-ifg-check-self! def-lrg n (ra-live-get (mut live) def-lrg))
                  (ra-live-set! (mut live) def-lrg 0))
                0)
            (if (or (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-PHI) (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-MEMPHI))
                0
                (do
                  (ra-ifg-kills! mach (mut live))
                  (if (!= def-lrg 0)
                      (let [(mut live-index) 0]
                        (loop (if (>= (load live-index) (len (.ids live)))
                                  (break 0)
                                  (let [other (ra-find! (get (.ids live) (load live-index)))]
                                    (if (and (!= (ra-live-get (mut live) other) 0)
                                             (!= other def-lrg))
                                        (match (ra-lrg-mask def-lrg)
                                          (Some [def-mask]
                                                (match (ra-lrg-mask other)
                                                  (Some [other-mask]
                                                        (if (mask-overlap? def-mask other-mask)
                                                            (match (m-outregmap mach)
                                                              (Some [out-mask]
                                                                    (if (mask-singleton? out-mask)
                                                                        (do
                                                                          (ra-lrg-deny-reg! other
                                                                                            (mask-first out-mask))
                                                                          0)
                                                                        (ra-ifg-add! def-lrg other)))
                                                              (None [] 0))
                                                            0))
                                                  (None [] 0)))
                                          (None [] 0))
                                        0)
                                    (set! (mut live-index) (+ (load live-index) 1))
                                    (continue)))))
                      0)
                  (let [(mut i) 1]
                    (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins n))
                              (break 0)
                              (do
                                (match (n-in n (load i))
                                  (Some [def]
                                        (let [input-lrg (ra-lrg-of! def)]
                                          (if (!= input-lrg 0)
                                              (do
                                                (ra-ifg-check-self! input-lrg
                                                                    def
                                                                    (ra-live-get (mut live)
                                                                                 input-lrg))
                                                (match (m-regmap mach (load i))
                                                  (Some [use-mask]
                                                        (if (mask-singleton? use-mask)
                                                            (let [(mut live-index) 0]
                                                              (loop (if (>= (load live-index)
                                                                            (len (.ids live)))
                                                                        (break 0)
                                                                        (let [other
                                                                                (ra-find! (get (.ids live)
                                                                                               (load live-index)))]
                                                                          (if (and (!= other input-lrg)
                                                                                   (!= (ra-live-get (mut live)
                                                                                                    other)
                                                                                       0))
                                                                              (do
                                                                                (ra-lrg-deny-reg! other
                                                                                                  (mask-first use-mask))
                                                                                0)
                                                                              0)
                                                                          (set! (mut live-index)
                                                                                (+ (load live-index)
                                                                                   1))
                                                                          (continue)))))
                                                            0))
                                                  (None [] 0))
                                                (ra-live-set! (mut live)
                                                              input-lrg
                                                              (n-nid def)))
                                              0)))
                                  (None [] 0))
                                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                (continue)))))
                  0))))))

(defn ra-ifg-block-of [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [id (n-block-nid n)]
    (match (arena-node id)
      (Some [block] block)
      (None [] (do (n-panic! "ra-ifg-block-of: the node was never placed in a block" n) (unreachable-node))))))

(defn ra-ifg-edge-def [(current (dyn NodeOps)) (arm i64) (def-id i64)] (-> i64)
  (match (arena-node def-id)
    (None [] def-id)
    (Some [def]
          (match (mach-of def)
            (Some [mach]
                  (if (and (or (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-PHI) (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-MEMPHI))
                           (= (n-block-nid def) (n-nid current))
                           (> arm 0)
                           (< arm (n-nins def)))
                      (match (n-in def arm) (Some [input] (n-nid input)) (None [] def-id))
                      def-id))
            (None [] def-id)))))

(defn ra-ifg-merge-def! [(block (dyn NodeOps)) (lrg i64) (def-id i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        block-id (n-nid block)
        key (ra-live-key block-id lrg)]
    (match (get (.liveouts (ra-state)) key)
      (None []
            (do
              (set! (mut (.liveouts state)) key def-id)
              (let [edge (len (.liveout-lrgs state))]
                (push! [i64] (mut (.liveout-lrgs state)) lrg)
                (push! [i64] (mut (.liveout-next state)) (get (.liveout-heads state) block-id))
                (set! (mut (.liveout-heads state)) block-id edge))
              true))
      (Some [prior-id]
            (do
              (if (!= prior-id def-id)
                  (match (arena-node def-id)
                    (Some [def] (ra-ifg-check-self! lrg def prior-id))
                    (None [] 0))
                  0)
              false)))))

(defn ra-ifg-merge-live! [(current (dyn NodeOps))
                          (pred (dyn NodeOps))
                          (arm i64)
                          (live (mut RaLive))] (-> i64)
  (let [block (ra-ifg-block-of pred)
        (mut changed) false
        (mut live-index) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load live-index) (len (.ids live)))
              (break 0)
              (let [lrg (ra-find! (get (.ids live) (load live-index)))
                    live-def (ra-live-get (mut live) lrg)]
                (if (!= live-def 0)
                    (let [def-id (ra-ifg-edge-def current arm live-def)
                          inserted (ra-ifg-merge-def! block lrg def-id)]
                      (if inserted (set! (mut changed) true) 0))
                    0)
                (set! (mut live-index) (+ (load live-index) 1))
                (continue))))
    ;; Phi arms are implicit uses on their matching predecessor edges. A backwards walk kills the
    ;; Phi definition at the merge head, so these edge uses must be added explicitly. In
    ;; particular, a loop-invariant backedge arm remains live through the cold entry edge; merging
    ;; it with a different entry arm in the shared Phi LRG records the self-conflict that drives
    ;; Simple's cold-then-hot edge splitting.
    (let [(mut si) 1]
      (loop (if (>= (load si) (code-schedule-count current))
                (break 0)
                (let [phi (code-schedule-at current (load si))]
                  (if (and (ra-phi? phi) (> arm 0) (< arm (n-nins phi)))
                      (match (n-in phi arm)
                        (Some [input]
                              (let [input-lrg (ra-lrg-of! input)]
                                (if (and (!= input-lrg 0)
                                         (ra-ifg-merge-def! block
                                                            input-lrg
                                                            (n-nid input)))
                                    (set! (mut changed) true)
                                    0)))
                        (None [] 0))
                      0)
                  (set! (mut si) (+ (load si) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    (if (load changed) (ra-ifg-push-work! block) 0)
    0))

(defn ra-ifg-propagate! [(block (dyn NodeOps)) (live (mut RaLive))] (-> i64)
  (match (mach-of block)
    (None [] 0)
    (Some [mach]
          (let [op (m-ideal-op mach)]
            (if (or (= op OP-START) (= op OP-FUN))
                0
                (if (or (= op OP-REGION) (= op OP-LOOP) (= op OP-STOP))
                    (let [(mut i) 1]
                      (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins block))
                                (break 0)
                                (do
                                  (match (n-in block (load i))
                                    (Some [pred]
                                          (ra-ifg-merge-live! block pred (load i) (mut live)))
                                    (None [] 0))
                                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                  (continue)))))
                    (match (n-in block 0)
                      (Some [pred] (ra-ifg-merge-live! block pred 0 (mut live)))
                      (None [] 0))))))))

;; Phi definitions happen in parallel at a Region head. Distinct surviving Phi results therefore
;; overlap at their definition point and cannot share a register. Simple's backwards IFG walk
;; obtains the same constraint from the simultaneously live Phi ranges; recording it explicitly
;; keeps that invariant independent of Coil's schedule order and eager use-count reclamation.
(defn ra-ifg-interfere-phis! [(block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut i) 1]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) (code-schedule-count block))
              (break 0)
              (let [left (code-schedule-at block (load i))]
                (if (or (= (ra-ideal-op left) OP-PHI) (= (ra-ideal-op left) OP-MEMPHI))
                    (let [(mut j) (+ (load i) 1)]
                      (loop (if (>= (load j) (code-schedule-count block))
                                (break 0)
                                (let [right (code-schedule-at block (load j))]
                                  (if (or (= (ra-ideal-op right) OP-PHI)
                                          (= (ra-ideal-op right) OP-MEMPHI))
                                      (let [left-lrg (ra-lrg-of! left)
                                            right-lrg (ra-lrg-of! right)]
                                        (if (and (!= left-lrg 0) (!= right-lrg 0))
                                            (match (ra-lrg-mask left-lrg)
                                              (Some [left-mask]
                                                    (match (ra-lrg-mask right-lrg)
                                                      (Some [right-mask]
                                                            (if (mask-overlap? left-mask right-mask)
                                                                (ra-ifg-add! left-lrg right-lrg)
                                                                0))
                                                      (None [] 0)))
                                              (None [] 0))
                                            0))
                                      0)
                                  (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                                  (continue)))))
                    0)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))))

(defn ra-ifg-do-block! [(block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut live) (ra-ifg-live-new block)
        (mut i) (- (code-schedule-count block) 1)]
    (ra-ifg-interfere-phis! block)
    ;; The head itself is structural; its kill mask (not its ordinary inputs) is applied after the
    ;; body walk, exactly where CallEnd clobbers become live-across-call constraints.
    (loop (if (<= (load i) 0)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (ra-ifg-node! (code-schedule-at block (load i)) (mut live))
                (set! (mut i) (- (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (match (mach-of block) (Some [mach] (ra-ifg-kills! mach (mut live))) (None [] 0))
    (ra-ifg-propagate! block (mut live))
    0))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The top driver
(defn ra-enclosing-fun [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (let [(mut cur) (Some n)
        (mut steps) 0
        limit (+ (arena-node-count) 1)
        (mut answer) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])]
    (loop (if (or (>= (load steps) limit)
                  (match (load cur) (Some [_] false) (None [] true))
                  (match (load answer) (Some [_] true) (None [] false)))
              (break 0)
              (match (load cur)
                (Some [c]
                      (if (= (ra-ideal-op c) OP-FUN)
                          (set! (mut answer) (Some c))
                          (do
                            (set! (mut cur) (cfg-idom-of c))
                            (set! (mut steps) (+ (load steps) 1))
                            (continue))))
                (None [] (break 0)))))
    (load answer)))

(defn ra-return-has-callee-save? [(ret (dyn NodeOps)) (reg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [(mut i) 1
        (mut found) false]
    (loop (if (or (>= (load i) (n-nins ret)) (load found))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (n-in ret (load i))
                  (Some [n]
                        (match (mach-of n)
                          (Some [mach]
                                (if (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-MACH-CALLEE-SAVE)
                                    (match (m-outregmap mach)
                                      (Some [mask]
                                            (if (and (mask-singleton? mask)
                                                     (= (mask-first mask) reg))
                                                (set! (mut found) true)
                                                0))
                                      (None [] 0))
                                    0))
                          (None [] 0)))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load found)))

;; Materialize ABI preservation before BuildLRG, exactly as final Simple does. Every register that
;; is neither caller-save nor reserved becomes a fixed live range from Fun to Return. Re-running
;; allocation is idempotent: existing fixed-register inputs are detected rather than duplicated.
(defn ra-insert-callee-saves! [] (-> i64)
  (let [caller (mach-active-caller-save)
        never (mach-active-never-save)
        max-reg (mach-active-max-reg)
        (mut ci) 0
        (mut count) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load ci) (code-cfg-count))
              (break 0)
              (let [ret (code-cfg-at (load ci))]
                (if (= (ra-ideal-op ret) OP-RETURN)
                    (match (ra-enclosing-fun ret)
                      (Some [fun]
                            (let [(mut reg) 0]
                              (loop (if (>= (load reg) max-reg)
                                        (break 0)
                                        (do
                                          (if (and (not (mask-test caller (load reg)))
                                                   (not (mask-test never (load reg)))
                                                   (not (ra-return-has-callee-save? ret
                                                                                    (load reg))))
                                              (let [save
                                                      (mach-make-callee-save fun
                                                                             ret
                                                                             (load reg))]
                                                ;; Final Simple inserts CalleeSave directly in the
                                                ;; Fun block's member list. Our schedules are
                                                ;; separate from def-use outs, so install the same
                                                ;; placement facts explicitly before rescheduling.
                                                ;; Without this, Return creates the LRG from its use
                                                ;; mask but the fixed definition is never visited;
                                                ;; splitting cannot legally place the entry-side
                                                ;; move and allocation cannot converge.
                                                (n-set-block-nid! save (n-nid fun))
                                                (n-set-early-nid! save (n-nid fun))
                                                (n-set-ltree-head! save (n-ltree-head fun))
                                                (n-set-ltree-parent! save (n-ltree-parent fun))
                                                (n-set-ltree-depth! save (n-ltree-depth fun))
                                                (set! (mut count) (+ (load count) 1)))
                                              0)
                                          (set! (mut reg) (+ (load reg) 1))
                                          (continue))))))
                      (None [] (panic "ra-insert-callee-saves!: Return has no enclosing Fun")))
                    0)
                (set! (mut ci) (+ (load ci) 1))
                (continue))))
    (if (> (load count) 0) (sched-run!) 0)
    (load count)))

;; Insert CalleeSave nodes, cache register masks for New and Call, then round after round of
;; colour-or-split until coloured or the budget is exhausted.
;; `AOT_RA_TRACE=1` narrates each failed round: the first failing live range, what it is, and the
;; split policy applied. Diagnostic only; never changes the allocation.
(defn ra-trace? [] (-> bool)
  (!= (primitive/cast i64 (os/getenv c"AOT_RA_TRACE")) 0))

(defn ra-trace-lrg! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> i64)
  (if (not (ra-trace?))
      0
      (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
            state (ra-state)]
        (println "ra: round {} failing lrg {} kind {} root-restricted {} mask-empty {} fixed-defs {} fixed-uses {} multi-defs {} self-conflict {}"
                 round leader (ra-lrg-kind leader)
                 (if (get (.root-restricted state) leader) 1 0)
                 (if (ra-lrg-mask-empty? leader) 1 0)
                 (get (.fixed-def-counts state) leader)
                 (get (.fixed-use-counts state) leader)
                 (if (get (.multi-defs state) leader) 1 0)
                 (if (ra-lrg-has-self-conflict? leader) 1 0))
        ;; The neighbours that deny it registers.
        (let [(mut edge) (get (.adj-heads state) leader)]
          (loop (if (< (load edge) 0)
                    (break 0)
                    (let [other (ra-find! (get (.adj-to state) (load edge)))]
                      (match (arena-node (ra-lrg-sample-nid other))
                        (Some [sample]
                              (do (println "    neighbour lrg {} reg {} kind {} : {s}"
                                           other (ra-lrg-reg other) (ra-lrg-kind other) (n-text sample))
                                  0))
                        (None [] 0))
                      (set! (mut edge) (get (.adj-next state) (load edge)))
                      (continue)))))
        (let [(mut nid) 1]
          (loop (if (> (load nid) (arena-node-count))
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (match (arena-node (load nid))
                        (Some [n]
                              (if (and (!= (n-lrg n) 0) (not (n-dead? n)) (= (ra-find! (n-lrg n)) leader))
                                  (let [(mut oi) 0]
                                    (println "    member: {s}" (n-text n))
                                    (loop (if (>= (load oi) (n-nouts n))
                                              (break 0)
                                              (do
                                                (match (n-out n (load oi))
                                                  (Some [use_] (do (println "      use: {s} (before-use -> {}, after-def -> {})" (n-text use_)
                                                                            (code-before-use-target use_) (code-after-def-target use_)) 0))
                                                  (None [] 0))
                                                (set! (mut oi) (+ (load oi) 1))
                                                (continue))))
                                    (match (arena-node (n-block-nid n))
                                      (Some [block]
                                            (let [(mut si) 0]
                                              (loop (if (>= (load si) (code-schedule-count block))
                                                        (break 0)
                                                        (do
                                                          (println "      sched[{}]: {s}" (load si) (n-text (code-schedule-at block (load si))))
                                                          (set! (mut si) (+ (load si) 1))
                                                          (continue))))))
                                      (None [] 0))
                                    0)
                                  0))
                        (None [] 0))
                      (set! (mut nid) (+ (load nid) 1))
                      (continue)))))
        0)))

(defn ra-run! [] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut round) 0]
    (ra-insert-callee-saves!)
    (loop (if (ra-graph-colour! (load round))
              (break 0)
              (let [leader (ra-find! (ra-first-failed))
                    sample (ra-lrg-sample-nid leader)]
                (ra-trace-lrg! (load round) leader)
                (if (>= (load round) (- RA-MAX-ROUNDS 1))
                    (match (arena-node sample)
                      (Some [n] (n-panic! "ra-run!: allocator exceeded its split budget; a live range of this node still fails" n))
                      (None [] (panic-i "ra-run!: allocator exceeded budget; sample nid" sample)))
                    0)
                (let [count (ra-split-all! (load round))]
                  (if (= count 0)
                      (panic-i "ra-run!: failed round produced no split; sample nid" sample)
                      0)
                  (set! (mut round) (+ (load round) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    (ra-post-colour!)
    (load round)))

;; One round: BuildLRG, then IFG build, then coalesce, then colour. Returns true when coloured.
;; Short-circuits: a hard register conflict in BuildLRG means there is no point building the IFG.
(defn ra-graph-colour! [(round i64)] (-> bool)
  (if (not (ra-build-lrg! round))
      false
      (if (not (ra-build-ifg! round))
          false
          ;; Coalescing is deliberately between IFG construction and simplify/color. Until the
          ;; copy-specific implementation below can prove a merge conservative, it changes none.
          (if (not (ra-coalesce! round)) false (ra-colour! round)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The four stages

;; Build live ranges and intersect their allowed register sets. Fails the round on a live range
;; whose allowed set is empty — a hard conflict, which is pre-split before anything else runs.
(defn ra-build-lrg! [(round i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [(mut ci) 0]
    (ra-reset-state! round)
    (loop (if (>= (load ci) (code-cfg-count))
              (break 0)
              (let [block (code-cfg-at (load ci))]
                (if (cfg-block-head-of? block)
                    (let [(mut i) 0]
                      (loop (if (>= (load i) (code-schedule-count block))
                                (break 0)
                                (do
                                  (ra-build-node! (code-schedule-at block (load i)))
                                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                  (continue)))))
                    0)
                (set! (mut ci) (+ (load ci) 1))
                (continue))))
    (ra-check-defined-lrgs!)
    (ra-compress-node-lrgs!)
    (ra-success?)))

;; A register operand names a value some scheduled machine node must define into a register class.
;; A live range with uses and no machine definition would be coloured from its uses alone and read
;; from a location nothing ever writes; a selected placeholder with no register class is the way
;; that happens, so it is a hard error here rather than a wrong answer at run time.
(defn ra-check-defined-lrgs! [] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        (mut id) 1]
    (loop (if (> (load id) (arena-node-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load id))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (and (!= (n-lrg n) 0)
                                 (= (get (.mach-defs state) (ra-find! (n-lrg n))) 0))
                            (n-panic! "ra-build-lrg!: a live range is used in a register but has no machine definition" n)
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                (continue))))
    0))

;; Build the interference graph — liveness and interference in ONE pass. A single-register def or
;; use DENIES its register to neighbours rather than adding an edge.
(defn ra-build-ifg! [(round i64)] (-> bool)
  (do
    round
    (set! (.ifg-build-count (ra-state)) (+ (.ifg-build-count (ra-state)) 1))
    (hm-clear! [i64 i64] (mut (.liveouts (ra-state))))
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.liveout-lrgs (ra-state))))
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.liveout-next (ra-state))))
    (hm-clear! [i64 bool] (mut (.ifg (ra-state))))
    (hm-clear! [i64 bool] (mut (.self-conflicts (ra-state))))
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.adj-to (ra-state))))
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.adj-next (ra-state))))
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.work (ra-state))))
    (let [(mut i) 0]
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (.adj-heads (ra-state))))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (set! (mut (.adj-heads (ra-state))) (load i) -1)
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue))))
      (set! (mut i) 0)
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (.liveout-heads (ra-state))))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (set! (mut (.liveout-heads (ra-state))) (load i) -1)
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue))))
      (set! (mut i) 0)
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (.on-work (ra-state))))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (set! (mut (.on-work (ra-state))) (load i) false)
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue))))
      (set! (mut i) 0)
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (code-cfg-count))
                (break 0)
                (let [cfg (code-cfg-at (load i))]
                  (if (cfg-block-head-of? cfg) (ra-ifg-push-work! cfg) 0)
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    (loop (match (ra-ifg-pop-work!)
            (None [] (break 0))
            (Some [block] (do (ra-ifg-do-block! block) (continue)))))
    (ra-success?)))

(defn ra-colour-capacity [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (match (ra-lrg-mask id)
    (None [] 0)
    (Some [mask] (let [size (mask-size mask)] (if (= size -1) 0x3fffffffffffffff size)))))

;; Final Simple scores a risky LRG by scheduled area recovered divided by loop-scaled split cost.
;; Whole-function CalleeSave ranges and separated cloneable definitions have concrete estimates;
;; the fallback slightly disfavors multi-use ranges because they cost more copies to split.
(defn ra-lrg-has-callee-save-def? [(id i64)] (-> bool)
  (!= (get (.callee-save-defs (ra-state)) (ra-find! id)) 0))

(defn ra-lrg-is-split-callee-save? [(id i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        def-id (get (.split-defs state) leader)
        use-id (get (.split-uses state) leader)]
    (and (!= def-id 0)
         (and (!= use-id 0)
              (match (arena-node def-id)
                (Some [def]
                      (and (> (n-nins def) 1)
                           (and (= (ra-ideal-op (n-in! def 1)) OP-MACH-CALLEE-SAVE)
                                (match (arena-node use-id)
                                  (Some [use_]
                                        (and (> (n-nouts use_) 0)
                                             (match (n-out use_ 0)
                                               (Some [out] (= (ra-ideal-op out) OP-RETURN))
                                               (None [] false))))
                                  (None [] false)))))
                (None [] false))))))

(defn ra-loop-cost-nid [(nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (match (arena-node nid)
    (None [] 1)
    (Some [n]
          (let [depth (looptree-depth-of (ra-ifg-block-of n))
                (mut cost) 1
                (mut i) 0]
            ;; Each loop nesting level is eight times hotter, matching Simple's `1 << depth*3`.
            ;; Saturation keeps malformed/extreme graphs from overflowing the risk comparison.
            (loop (if (or (>= (load i) depth) (> (load cost) 0x0fffffffffffffff))
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (set! (mut cost) (* (load cost) 8))
                        (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                        (continue))))
            (load cost)))))

(defn ra-lrg-function [(id i64)] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        sample
          (let [def (get (.mach-defs state) leader)]
            (if (!= def 0)
                def
                (let [use (get (.mach-uses state) leader)]
                  (if (!= use 0) use (ra-lrg-sample-nid leader)))))]
    (match (arena-node sample)
      (Some [n] (ra-enclosing-fun (ra-ifg-block-of n)))
      (None [] (None [(dyn NodeOps)])))))

(defn ra-build-function-areas! [] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        (mut ci) 0]
    (if (not (.function-area-ready state))
        (do
          (loop (if (>= (load ci) (code-cfg-count))
                    (break 0)
                    (let [block (code-cfg-at (load ci))]
                      (set! (.function-area-block-visits state)
                            (+ (.function-area-block-visits state) 1))
                      (if (cfg-block-head-of? block)
                          (match (ra-enclosing-fun block)
                            (Some [owner]
                                  (let [key (n-nid owner)
                                        prior
                                          (match (get (.function-areas state) key)
                                            (Some [area] area)
                                            (None [] 0))]
                                    (set! (mut (.function-areas state))
                                          key
                                          (+ prior (code-schedule-count block)))))
                            (None [] 0))
                          0)
                      (set! (mut ci) (+ (load ci) 1))
                      (continue))))
          (set! (.function-area-ready state) true))
        0)
    (len (.function-areas state))))

(defn ra-function-area [(fun (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (do
    (ra-build-function-areas!)
    (match (get (.function-areas (ra-state)) (n-nid fun))
      (Some [area] area)
      (None [] 0))))

(defn ra-function-area-block-visits [] (-> i64)
  (.function-area-block-visits (ra-state)))

(defn ra-area-score [(area i64) (cost i64)] (-> i64)
  (+ 1000 (/ (* area 1024) (if (> cost 0) cost 1))))

(defn ra-block-schedule-index [(block (dyn NodeOps)) (nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut i) 0
        (mut answer) -1]
    (loop (if (or (>= (load i) (code-schedule-count block)) (>= (load answer) 0))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (= (n-nid (code-schedule-at block (load i))) nid)
                    (set! (mut answer) (load i))
                    0)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load answer)))

(defn ra-colour-risk-score [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        def-id (get (.mach-defs state) leader)
        use-id (get (.mach-uses state) leader)]
    (if (or (ra-lrg-has-callee-save-def? leader) (ra-lrg-is-split-callee-save? leader))
        (match (ra-lrg-function leader)
          (Some [fun]
                (ra-area-score (ra-function-area fun)
                               (if (ra-lrg-has-callee-save-def? leader)
                                   (+ (ra-loop-cost-nid (get (.callee-save-defs state) leader))
                                      (if (= use-id 0) 0 (ra-loop-cost-nid use-id)))
                                   (+ (ra-loop-cost-nid (get (.split-defs state) leader))
                                      (ra-loop-cost-nid (get (.split-uses state) leader))))))
          (None [] 2000))
        (if (and (not (get (.multi-defs state) leader))
                 (!= def-id 0)
                 (!= use-id 0)
                 (match (arena-node def-id)
                   (Some [def]
                         (match (mach-of def)
                           (Some [mach] (m-clone-cheap? mach))
                           (None [] false)))
                   (None [] false)))
            (match (arena-node def-id)
              (Some [def]
                    (match (arena-node use-id)
                      (Some [use_]
                            (let [def-block (ra-ifg-block-of def)
                                  use-block (ra-ifg-block-of use_)
                                  area
                                    (if (n-same? def-block use-block)
                                        (- (- (ra-block-schedule-index use-block use-id)
                                              (ra-block-schedule-index def-block def-id))
                                           1)
                                        (match (ra-lrg-function leader)
                                          (Some [fun] (ra-function-area fun))
                                          (None [] 0)))]
                              (if (> area 0)
                                  (ra-area-score area (ra-loop-cost-nid use-id))
                                  (- 1000
                                     (if (get (.multi-uses state) leader) 100 0)))))
                      (None [] (- 1000 (if (get (.multi-uses state) leader) 100 0)))))
              (None [] (- 1000 (if (get (.multi-uses state) leader) 100 0))))
            (- 1000 (if (get (.multi-uses state) leader) 100 0))))))

(defn ra-colour-has-split? [(id i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)]
    (or (!= (get (.split-defs state) leader) 0)
        (!= (get (.split-uses state) leader) 0))))

;; Final Simple orders every currently trivial range so reverse coloring sees fixed ranges first,
;; ordinary ranges next and Split-related ranges last, with the latter able to bias toward already
;; assigned colors. Return true exactly when `candidate` should leave the IFG before `best`.
(defn ra-colour-better? [(best i64) (candidate i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [best-size (ra-colour-capacity best)
        candidate-size (ra-colour-capacity candidate)
        best-single (= best-size 1)
        candidate-single (= candidate-size 1)
        best-split (ra-colour-has-split? best)
        candidate-split (ra-colour-has-split? candidate)]
    (if (!= best-single candidate-single)
        best-single
        (if (!= best-split candidate-split)
            candidate-split
            (if best-single
                (and (not (get (.multi-uses (ra-state)) (ra-find! best)))
                     (get (.multi-uses (ra-state)) (ra-find! candidate)))
                (< best-size candidate-size))))))

(defn ra-colour-low-sift-up! [(start i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [work (.colour-low-work (ra-state))
        (mut child) start]
    (loop (if (<= (load child) 0)
              (break 0)
              (let [parent (/ (- (load child) 1) 2)
                    child-id (get work (load child))
                    parent-id (get work parent)]
                (if (ra-colour-better? parent-id child-id)
                    (do
                      (set! (mut (.colour-low-work (ra-state))) (load child) parent-id)
                      (set! (mut (.colour-low-work (ra-state))) parent child-id)
                      (set! (mut child) parent)
                      (continue))
                    (break 0)))))
    0))

(defn ra-colour-low-sift-down! [(start i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [work (.colour-low-work (ra-state))
        (mut root) start]
    (loop (let [left (+ (* (load root) 2) 1)]
            (if (>= left (len work))
                (break 0)
                (let [(mut best) (load root)
                      right (+ left 1)]
                  (if (ra-colour-better? (get work (load best)) (get work left))
                      (set! (mut best) left)
                      0)
                  (if (and (< right (len work))
                           (ra-colour-better? (get work (load best)) (get work right)))
                      (set! (mut best) right)
                      0)
                  (if (= (load best) (load root))
                      (break 0)
                      (let [root-id (get work (load root))]
                        (set! (mut (.colour-low-work (ra-state)))
                              (load root)
                              (get work (load best)))
                        (set! (mut (.colour-low-work (ra-state))) (load best) root-id)
                        (set! (mut root) (load best))
                        (continue)))))))
    0))

(defn ra-colour-low-push! [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)]
    (if (or (get (.removed state) id) (get (.colour-low-on state) id))
        0
        (do
          (set! (mut (.colour-low-on state)) id true)
          (push! [i64] (mut (.colour-low-work state)) id)
          (ra-colour-low-sift-up! (- (len (.colour-low-work state)) 1))))))

(defn ra-colour-low-pop! [] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        work (.colour-low-work state)]
    (if (= (len work) 0)
        0
        (let [answer (get work 0)]
          (match (pop! [i64] (mut (.colour-low-work state)))
            (Some [last]
                  (if (> (len (.colour-low-work state)) 0)
                      (do
                        (set! (mut (.colour-low-work state)) 0 last)
                        (ra-colour-low-sift-down! 0))
                      0))
            (None [] 0))
          answer))))

(defn ra-colour-init! [] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        (mut id) 1]
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.color-stack state)))
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.colour-low-work state)))
    (loop (if (> (load id) (ra-lrg-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (set! (mut (.degree state))
                      (load id)
                      (if (= (ra-find! (load id)) (load id)) (ra-adj-degree (load id)) 0))
                (set! (mut (.removed state)) (load id) false)
                (set! (mut (.regs state)) (load id) -1)
                (set! (mut (.colour-low-on state)) (load id) false)
                (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                (continue))))
    (set! (mut id) 1)
    (loop (if (> (load id) (ra-lrg-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (and (= (ra-find! (load id)) (load id))
                         (< (get (.degree state) (load id)) (ra-colour-capacity (load id))))
                    (ra-colour-low-push! (load id))
                    0)
                (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                (continue))))
    0))

(defn ra-colour-pick! [] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        (mut id) 1
        (mut risky) 0
        (mut risky-score) -1
        low
          (loop (let [candidate (ra-colour-low-pop!)]
                  (if (= candidate 0)
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (set! (mut (.colour-low-on state)) candidate false)
                        (if (and (= (ra-find! candidate) candidate)
                                 (not (get (.removed state) candidate))
                                 (< (get (.degree state) candidate)
                                    (ra-colour-capacity candidate)))
                            (break candidate)
                            (continue))))))]
    (if (!= low 0)
        low
        (do
          ;; Only a non-trivial clique needs a global risk comparison.
          (loop (if (> (load id) (ra-lrg-count))
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (if (and (= (ra-find! (load id)) (load id))
                               (not (get (.removed state) (load id))))
                          (let [score (ra-colour-risk-score (load id))]
                            (if (or (= (load risky) 0) (> score (load risky-score)))
                                (do
                                  (set! (mut risky) (load id))
                                  (set! (mut risky-score) score))
                                0))
                          0)
                      (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                      (continue))))
          (load risky)))))

(defn ra-colour-remove! [(id i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        (mut edge) (get (.adj-heads (ra-state)) id)]
    (set! (mut (.removed state)) id true)
    (push! [i64] (mut (.color-stack state)) id)
    (loop (if (< (load edge) 0)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (let [raw-other (get (.adj-to state) (load edge))]
                  (if (> raw-other 0)
                      (let [other (ra-find! raw-other)]
                        (if (and (!= other id) (not (get (.removed state) other)))
                            (let [degree (get (.degree state) other)]
                              (if (<= degree 0)
                                  (broken "ra-colour-remove!: degree underflow")
                                  (do
                                    (set! (mut (.degree state)) other (- degree 1))
                                    (if (< (- degree 1) (ra-colour-capacity other))
                                        (ra-colour-low-push! other)
                                        0))))
                            0))
                      0))
                (set! (mut edge) (get (.adj-next state) (load edge)))
                (continue))))
    0))

(defn ra-biasable-input-index [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (= (n-op n) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
      1
      (match (mach-of n)
        (None [] 0)
        (Some [mach]
              (let [op (m-ideal-op mach)]
                (if (or (= op OP-PHI) (= op OP-MEMPHI))
                    (if (and (> (n-nins n) 0)
                             (match (mach-of (n-in! n 0))
                               (Some [ctrl] (= (m-ideal-op ctrl) OP-LOOP))
                               (None [] false)))
                        2
                        1)
                    (m-two-address mach)))))))

(defn ra-bias-trim-neighbors! [(id i64) (choices (mut (ptr RegMask)))] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        (mut edge) (get (.adj-heads state) leader)]
    (loop (if (< (load edge) 0)
              (break -1)
              (let [raw (get (.adj-to state) (load edge))]
                (if (> raw 0)
                    (let [other (ra-find! raw)
                          assigned (get (.regs state) other)
                          forbidden
                            (if (>= assigned 0)
                                assigned
                                (match (ra-lrg-mask other)
                                  (Some [mask]
                                        (if (mask-singleton? mask) (mask-first mask) -1))
                                  (None [] -1)))]
                      (if (>= forbidden 0)
                          (let [trimmed (mask-sub (load choices) (mask-of forbidden))]
                            ;; Neighbor trimming is a preference, not an interference constraint.
                            ;; Never discard the last legal color for the LRG being colored.
                            (if (mask-empty? trimmed)
                                0
                                (do
                                  (set! choices trimmed)
                                  (if (mask-singleton? (load choices))
                                      (break (mask-first (load choices)))
                                      0))))
                          0))
                    0)
                (set! (mut edge) (get (.adj-next state) (load edge)))
                (continue))))))

;; Final Simple follows both sides of a Split/Phi/two-address chain for at most ten steps. Prefer an
;; already assigned color when legal; otherwise remove colors forced by already-colored or
;; singleton neighbors of the chain. This is what makes adjacent spill halves converge on the same
;; register often enough for post-color removal.
(defn ra-bias-colour [(id i64) (base (ptr RegMask))] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        (mut choices) base
        (mut def-id) (get (.split-defs state) leader)
        (mut use-id) (get (.split-uses state) leader)
        (mut count) 0
        (mut answer) -1]
    (loop (if (or (> (load count) 10)
                  (and (= (load def-id) 0) (= (load use-id) 0))
                  (>= (load answer) 0))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (!= (load def-id) 0)
                    (match (arena-node (load def-id))
                      (None [] (set! (mut def-id) 0))
                      (Some [def]
                            (let [chain-lrg (ra-lrg-of! def)
                                  assigned (if (= chain-lrg 0) -1 (get (.regs state) chain-lrg))
                                  advance (ra-biasable-input-index def)]
                              (if (>= assigned 0)
                                  (if (mask-test (load choices) assigned)
                                      (set! (mut answer) assigned)
                                      (set! (mut def-id) 0))
                                  (if (= advance 0) (set! (mut def-id) 0) 0)))))
                    0)
                (if (and (< (load answer) 0) (!= (load use-id) 0))
                    (match (arena-node (load use-id))
                      (None [] (set! (mut use-id) 0))
                      (Some [use_]
                            (let [chain-lrg (ra-lrg-of! use_)
                                  assigned (if (= chain-lrg 0) -1 (get (.regs state) chain-lrg))
                                  advance (ra-biasable-input-index use_)]
                              (if (>= assigned 0)
                                  (if (mask-test (load choices) assigned)
                                      (set! (mut answer) assigned)
                                      (set! (mut use-id) 0))
                                  (if (= advance 0) (set! (mut use-id) 0) 0)))))
                    0)
                (if (and (< (load answer) 0) (!= (load def-id) 0))
                    (match (arena-node (load def-id))
                      (None [] (set! (mut def-id) 0))
                      (Some [def]
                            (let [chain-lrg (ra-lrg-of! def)
                                  biased
                                    (if (= chain-lrg 0)
                                        -1
                                        (ra-bias-trim-neighbors! chain-lrg
                                                                 (mut choices)))]
                              (if (>= biased 0)
                                  (set! (mut answer) biased)
                                  (let [advance (ra-biasable-input-index def)]
                                    (if (and (> advance 0) (< advance (n-nins def)))
                                        (let [next (n-in! def advance)]
                                          (if (= (ra-lrg-of! next) 0)
                                              (set! (mut def-id) 0)
                                              (set! (mut def-id) (n-nid next))))
                                        (set! (mut def-id) 0)))))))
                    0)
                (if (and (< (load answer) 0) (!= (load use-id) 0))
                    (match (arena-node (load use-id))
                      (None [] (set! (mut use-id) 0))
                      (Some [use_]
                            (let [chain-lrg (ra-lrg-of! use_)
                                  biased
                                    (if (= chain-lrg 0)
                                        -1
                                        (ra-bias-trim-neighbors! chain-lrg
                                                                 (mut choices)))]
                              (if (>= biased 0)
                                  (set! (mut answer) biased)
                                  (if (= (n-nouts use_) 0)
                                      (set! (mut use-id) 0)
                                      (match (n-out use_ 0)
                                        (None [] (set! (mut use-id) 0))
                                        (Some [next]
                                              (if (= (ra-biasable-input-index next) 0)
                                                  (set! (mut use-id) 0)
                                                  (set! (mut use-id) (n-nid next))))))))))
                    0)
                (set! (mut count) (+ (load count) 1))
                (continue))))
    (if (>= (load answer) 0) (load answer) (mask-first (load choices)))))

(defn ra-colour-one! [(id i64)] (-> bool)
  (match (ra-lrg-mask id)
    (None [] (do (ra-fail! id) false))
    (Some [base]
          (let [(mut choices) base
                (mut edge) (get (.adj-heads (ra-state)) id)]
            (loop (if (< (load edge) 0)
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (let [raw-other (get (.adj-to (ra-state)) (load edge))]
                          (if (> raw-other 0)
                              (let [other (ra-find! raw-other)]
                                (if (and (!= other id)
                                         (>= (get (.regs (ra-state)) other) 0))
                                    (set! (mut choices)
                                          (mask-sub (load choices)
                                                    (mask-of (get (.regs (ra-state)) other))))
                                    0))
                              0))
                        (set! (mut edge) (get (.adj-next (ra-state)) (load edge)))
                        (continue))))
            (if (mask-empty? (load choices))
                (do (ra-fail! id) false)
                (do
                  (set! (mut (.regs (ra-state)))
                        id
                        (if (mask-singleton? (load choices))
                            (mask-first (load choices))
                            (ra-bias-colour id (load choices))))
                  true))))))

(defn ra-propagate-colours! [] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut nid) 1]
    (loop (if (> (load nid) (arena-node-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load nid))
                  (Some [n]
                        (let [lrg (ra-lrg-of! n)]
                          (if (= lrg 0)
                              (n-set-reg! n -1)
                              (n-set-reg! n (get (.regs (ra-state)) lrg)))))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut nid) (+ (load nid) 1))
                (continue))))
    0))

(defn ra-split-block-for-use [(use_ (dyn NodeOps)) (idx i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (match (mach-of use_)
    (Some [mach]
          (if (and (or (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-PHI) (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-MEMPHI))
                   (> idx 0))
              (let [region (n-in! use_ 0)
                    pred (n-in! region idx)]
                (ra-ifg-block-of pred))
              (ra-ifg-block-of use_)))
    (None []
          (do
            (panic "ra-split-block-for-use: use is not a machine node")
            (unreachable-node)))))

(defn ra-place-copy! [(copy (dyn NodeOps)) (block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (do
    (n-set-block-nid! copy (n-nid block))
    (n-set-early-nid! copy (n-nid block))
    0))

(defn ra-anchor-before-use! [(copy (dyn NodeOps))
                             (value (dyn NodeOps))
                             (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                             (block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  ;; Final Simple's `Node.insertBefore` edits the basic block's authoritative ordered list. Our
  ;; local schedule is a separate durable table, so record the same exact relation there; adding
  ;; graph dependencies cannot represent adjacency and allows later scheduling rounds to drift.
  (do value block 0)
  (if (ra-phi? use_) 0 (code-record-before-use! copy use_)))

;; Final Simple's makeSplit clones cheap machine definitions when their output mask can satisfy the
;; constrained use. This is not an optional peephole: repeatedly inserting a Split after a
;; cloneable Box leaves the same short fixed-register conflict for the next round. Re-materializing
;; the Box at the use shortens its source live range and makes allocation converge.
(defn ra-clone-compatible-with-use? [(value-mach (dyn MachNode))
                                     (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                                     (idx i64)] (-> bool)
  (match (m-outregmap value-mach)
    (None [] false)
    (Some [value-mask]
          (match (mach-of use_)
            (None [] false)
            (Some [use-mach]
                  (match (m-regmap use-mach idx)
                    (None [] false)
                    (Some [use-mask] (mask-overlap? value-mask use-mask))))))))

(defn ra-clone-crosses-use-clobber? [(value (dyn NodeOps))
                                     (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                                     (idx i64)] (-> bool)
  (if (= (n-block-nid value) 0)
      false
      (let [value-block (ra-ifg-block-of value)
            use-block (ra-split-block-for-use use_ idx)]
        (if (or (not (n-same? value-block use-block))
                (not (code-schedule-ready? value-block)))
            false
            (match (mach-of use_)
              (None [] false)
              (Some [use-mach]
                    (match (m-regmap use-mach idx)
                      (None [] false)
                      (Some [required]
                            (match (mach-of value)
                              (None [] false)
                              (Some [value-mach]
                                    (match (m-outregmap value-mach)
                                      (None [] false)
                                      (Some [produced]
                                            (let [from
                                                    (ra-block-schedule-index value-block
                                                                             (n-nid value))
                                                  to
                                                    (ra-block-schedule-index use-block
                                                                             (n-nid use_))
                                                  managed
                                                    (or (ty-memptr? (n-ty value))
                                                        (ty-dyn? (n-ty value)))
                                                  (mut remaining) (mask-and produced required)
                                                  (mut i) (+ from 1)]
                                              (if (or (< from 0) (<= to from))
                                                  false
                                                  (do
                                                    (loop (if (or (>= (load i) to)
                                                                  (mask-empty? (load remaining)))
                                                              (break 0)
                                                              (do
                                                                (match (mach-of (code-schedule-at use-block
                                                                                                  (load i)))
                                                                  (Some [between]
                                                                        (do
                                                                          (if (and managed
                                                                                   (or (= (m-ideal-op between)
                                                                                          OP-CALL)
                                                                                       (= (m-ideal-op between)
                                                                                          OP-NEW)
                                                                                       (= (m-ideal-op between)
                                                                                          OP-SAFEPOINT)))
                                                                              (set! (mut remaining)
                                                                                    (mask-and (load remaining)
                                                                                              (selected-gc-root-mask)))
                                                                              0)
                                                                          (match (m-killmap between)
                                                                            (Some [kills]
                                                                                  (set! (mut remaining)
                                                                                        (mask-sub (load remaining)
                                                                                                  kills)))
                                                                            (None [] 0))))
                                                                  (None [] 0))
                                                                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                                                (continue))))
                                                    (mask-empty? (load remaining)))))))))))))))))

(defn ra-bind-clone-at! [(copy (dyn NodeOps))
                         (value (dyn NodeOps))
                         (value-mach (dyn MachNode))
                         (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                         (block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (do
    ;; Target clones copy their raw input slots but have no output edges. Rebind through NodeOps so
    ;; def-use edges remain exact after RA.
    (if (!= (n-nouts copy) 0) (broken "ra-bind-clone-at!: fresh clone has outputs") 0)
    (loop (if (= (n-nins copy) 0)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (pop! (mut (.ins (hdr copy))))
                (continue))))
    (n-add-def! copy (Some block))
    (let [(mut input) 1]
      (loop (if (>= (load input) (n-nins value))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  ;; Do not inherit a scheduling-only anchor from an older rematerialization.
                  ;; Machine register inputs are the semantic operands; input zero is replaced by
                  ;; the placement control above.
                  (match (m-regmap value-mach (load input))
                    (Some [_] (n-add-def! copy (n-in value (load input))))
                    (None [] 0))
                  (set! (mut input) (+ (load input) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    (ra-anchor-before-use! copy value use_ block)
    (ra-place-copy! copy block)
    0))

(defn ra-clone-for-use [(value (dyn NodeOps))
                        (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                        (idx i64)
                        (block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (match (mach-of value)
    (None [] (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
    (Some [value-mach]
          (if (or (not (m-clone-cheap? value-mach))
                  (not (ra-clone-compatible-with-use? value-mach use_ idx))
                  (ra-clone-crosses-use-clobber? value use_ idx))
              (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
              (match (m-clone value-mach)
                (None []
                      (do
                        (panic "ra-clone-for-use: clone-cheap machine refused to clone")
                        (None [(dyn NodeOps)])))
                (Some [copy]
                      (do
                        (ra-bind-clone-at! copy value value-mach use_ block)
                        (Some copy))))))))

(defn ra-split-before-use-node-mode! [(round i64)
                                      (lrg i64)
                                      (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                                      (idx i64)
                                      (kind i64)
                                      (skip-old bool)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (or (< idx 1) (>= idx (n-nins use_)))
      (do
        (panic-i "ra-split-before-use-node-mode!: input index out of range" idx)
        (unreachable-node))
      (let [value
              (match (n-in use_ idx)
                (Some [input] input)
                (None []
                      (do
                        (panic-i "ra-split-before-use-node-mode!: selected input disappeared"
                                 (n-nid use_))
                        (unreachable-node))))
            block (ra-split-block-for-use use_ idx)]
        (match (ra-clone-for-use value use_ idx block)
          (Some [copy]
                (do
                  (n-set-def! use_ idx (Some copy))
                  ;; Replacing the final use of an earlier cheap rematerialization leaves that
                  ;; definition in the durable schedule unless we retire it explicitly. A dead
                  ;; clone would otherwise be rediscovered as a register-bearing definition in
                  ;; every allocation round and be rematerialized forever. Cheap machine nodes
                  ;; are pure by contract, so an empty output multiset makes this value dead.
                  (if (= (n-nouts value) 0) (n-kill! value) 0)
                  copy))
          (None []
                (let [split (mach-make-split lrg kind round block value)
                      ;; An older copy made for THIS use, in this block: the new copy replaces it
                      ;; (Simple's insertBefore bypasses it). Any other split — an after-definition
                      ;; copy moving a fixed-register value out of its register — is a value in
                      ;; its own right and stays in the chain; bypassing it undid it every round.
                      older-copy-for-use
                        (and skip-old
                             (= (n-op value) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                             (= (n-block-nid value) (n-nid block))
                             (= (code-before-use-target value) (n-nid use_)))]
                  (ra-place-copy! split block)
                  ;; The value may itself be a copy anchored before this use that we keep; its use
                  ;; is now the new split, and its anchor must say so, or the two race for the slot.
                  (if (and (not older-copy-for-use) (= (code-before-use-target value) (n-nid use_)))
                      (code-record-before-use! value split)
                      0)
                  ;; Final Simple's `insertBefore(use)`: the copy sits immediately before its use.
                  ;; Left to the list scheduler it floats up the block and may cross a safepoint
                  ;; (a runtime property store, an allocation) between it and the use; a managed
                  ;; copy live across a safepoint must live on the stack, which a register copy
                  ;; cannot, and every later round re-makes the same copy in the same place.
                  (ra-anchor-before-use! split value use_ block)
                  (n-set-def! use_ idx (Some split))
                  ;; Simple's insertBefore bypasses an older same-block Split after placing the new
                  ;; one. Rebinding after the use moves preserves the old Split until the new input
                  ;; is ready, then ordinary last-use death removes the obsolete copy.
                  (if older-copy-for-use
                      (n-set-def! split 1 (Some (n-in! value 1)))
                      0)
                  split))))))

(defn ra-split-before-use-node! [(round i64)
                                 (lrg i64)
                                 (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                                 (idx i64)
                                 (kind i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (ra-split-before-use-node-mode! round lrg use_ idx kind true))

(defn ra-split-after-def-node! [(round i64)
                                (lrg i64)
                                (def (dyn NodeOps))
                                (kind i64)] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut uses) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut indices) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut seen-uses) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a)
        (mut oi) 0]
    ;; Snapshot every register-bearing use before constructing the split, because binding the split
    ;; itself adds a new output and every subsequent n-set-def! mutates this def's output multiset.
    (loop (if (>= (load oi) (n-nouts def))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (n-out def (load oi))
                  (Some [use_]
                        (ra-snapshot-register-use! def
                                                   use_
                                                   (mut uses)
                                                   (mut indices)
                                                   (mut seen-uses)))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut oi) (+ (load oi) 1))
                (continue))))
    (let [block (ra-ifg-block-of def)
          split (mach-make-split lrg kind round block def)
          (mut i) 0]
      (ra-place-copy! split block)
      (code-record-after-def! split def)
      (if (ra-trace?)
          (do (println "ra:   after-def split {s} rewiring {} uses" (n-text split) (len (load uses))) 0)
          0)
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (load uses)))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (match (arena-node (get (load uses) (load i)))
                    (Some [use_] (n-set-def! use_ (get (load indices) (load i)) (Some split)))
                    (None [] (panic "ra-split-after-def-node!: snapshotted use disappeared")))
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue))))
      split)))

;; Count the distinct leaders adjacent to either side of a proposed merge. The direct edge between
;; the pair is ignored here; callers reject it before asking for capacity.
(defn ra-coalesce-degree [(a i64) (b i64)] (-> i64)
  (ra-adj-union-degree a b))

(defn ra-forget-coalesced-split! [(id i64) (split (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! id)
        nid (n-nid split)]
    (if (= (get (.mach-defs state) leader) nid)
        (set! (mut (.mach-defs state)) leader 0)
        0)
    (if (= (get (.mach-uses state) leader) nid)
        (do
          (set! (mut (.mach-uses state)) leader 0)
          (set! (mut (.mach-use-inputs state)) leader 0))
        0)
    (if (= (get (.split-defs state) leader) nid)
        (set! (mut (.split-defs state)) leader 0)
        0)
    (if (= (get (.split-uses state) leader) nid)
        (set! (mut (.split-uses state)) leader 0)
        0)
    0))

;; Final Simple discovers copies from the authoritative per-block instruction lists. Walking those
;; durable schedules keeps coalescing and postcolor proportional to emitted work, independent of
;; dead declarations or disconnected constants retained elsewhere in the compilation arena.
(defn ra-snapshot-scheduled-splits [] (-> (ArrayList i64))
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut splits) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut ci) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load ci) (code-cfg-count))
              (break 0)
              (let [block (code-cfg-at (load ci))]
                (if (cfg-block-head-of? block)
                    (let [(mut i) 0]
                      (loop (if (>= (load i) (code-schedule-count block))
                                (break 0)
                                (let [n (code-schedule-at block (load i))]
                                  (if (and (not (n-dead? n))
                                           (= (n-op n) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                                           (> (n-nins n) 1))
                                      (push! [i64] (mut splits) (n-nid n))
                                      0)
                                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                  (continue)))))
                    0)
                (set! (mut ci) (+ (load ci) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load splits)))

;; Coalesce Split copies conservatively, following Simple's guards in order: the halves must be
;; distinct, non-interfering, have overlapping masks, and the merged neighborhood must remain
;; trivially colourable. Final Simple grows the larger adjacency with the smaller, unions the LRGs,
;; then replaces the losing LRG in every neighbor. `ra-ifg-merge-adjacency!` performs that mutation
;; directly: coalescing many copies is proportional to their incident edges, never one full liveness
;; and IFG rebuild per copy.
(defn ra-coalesce! [(round i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        splits (ra-snapshot-scheduled-splits)
        (mut remove) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut progress) false]
    (do round 0)
    (let [(mut i) 0]
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (len splits))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (match (arena-node (get splits (load i)))
                    (Some [split]
                          (if (and (not (n-dead? split))
                                   (> (n-nins split) 1)
                                   (> (n-lrg split) 0)
                                   (> (n-lrg (n-in! split 1)) 0))
                              (let [left (ra-lrg-of! split)
                                    right (ra-lrg-of! (n-in! split 1))]
                                (if (= left right)
                                    (do
                                      (if (ra-trace?)
                                          (do (println "ra:   redundant split {s} (lrg {})" (n-text split) left) 0)
                                          0)
                                      (ra-forget-coalesced-split! left split)
                                      (push! [i64] (mut remove) (n-nid split)))
                                    (if (not (ra-ifg-interferes? left right))
                                        (match (ra-lrg-mask left)
                                          (Some [left-mask]
                                                (match (ra-lrg-mask right)
                                                  (Some [right-mask]
                                                        (let [merged-mask (mask-and left-mask right-mask)
                                                              capacity (mask-size merged-mask)]
                                                          (if (and (not (mask-empty? merged-mask))
                                                                   (or (= capacity -1)
                                                                       (< (ra-coalesce-degree left right)
                                                                          capacity)))
                                                              (do
                                                                ;; Remove dying endpoint evidence
                                                                ;; before union, as final Simple
                                                                ;; does, so the other side's bias
                                                                ;; metadata survives the fold.
                                                                (ra-forget-coalesced-split! left
                                                                                            split)
                                                                (ra-forget-coalesced-split! right
                                                                                            split)
                                                                (let [winner (ra-union! left right)
                                                                      loser
                                                                        (if (= winner left)
                                                                            right
                                                                            left)]
                                                                  (if (ra-trace?)
                                                                      (do (println "ra:   coalesced {s} (lrgs {} {})" (n-text split) left right) 0)
                                                                      0)
                                                                  (ra-ifg-merge-adjacency! winner
                                                                                           loser)
                                                                  (push! [i64]
                                                                         (mut remove)
                                                                         (n-nid split))
                                                                  (set! (mut progress) true)))
                                                              0)))
                                                  (None [] 0)))
                                          (None [] 0))
                                        0)))
                              0))
                    (None [] 0))
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    (if (load progress) (ra-compress-node-lrgs!) 0)
    (let [(mut i) 0]
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (load remove)))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (match (arena-node (get (load remove) (load i)))
                    (Some [split]
                          (if (and (not (n-dead? split))
                                   (= (n-op split) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                                   (> (n-nins split) 1))
                              (n-subsume! split (n-in! split 1))
                              0))
                    (None [] 0))
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    ;; Final Simple removes the Split from the block's authoritative output list immediately.
    ;; Our schedule is durable and separate from def-use outs, so refresh it after graph removal;
    ;; otherwise dead zero-input Split entries reach layout and dereference a missing value input.
    (if (> (len (load remove)) 0) (code-schedule-compact!) 0)
    (ra-success?)))

;; Colour: remove trivially-colourable nodes first, then any, until the graph is empty; then assign
;; colours in reverse removal order. False if some live range could not be coloured.
(defn ra-colour! [(round i64)] (-> bool)
  (do
    round
    (ra-colour-init!)
    (let [(mut remaining) 0
          (mut id) 1]
      (loop (if (> (load id) (ra-lrg-count))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (if (= (ra-find! (load id)) (load id))
                      (set! (mut remaining) (+ (load remaining) 1))
                      0)
                  (set! (mut id) (+ (load id) 1))
                  (continue))))
      (loop (if (= (load remaining) 0)
                (break 0)
                (let [pick (ra-colour-pick!)]
                  (if (= pick 0)
                      (do (broken "ra-colour!: simplify lost a live range") (break 0))
                      (do
                        (ra-colour-remove! pick)
                        (set! (mut remaining) (- (load remaining) 1))
                        (continue)))))))
    (loop (match (pop! [i64] (mut (.color-stack (ra-state))))
            (None [] (break 0))
            (Some [id] (do (ra-colour-one! id) (continue)))))
    (ra-propagate-colours!)
    (ra-success?)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Splitting

;; Split every failed live range. Sorted by live-range id so that splitting is DETERMINISTIC —
;; an allocator whose output depends on hash order is not reproducible, and a golden test over it
;; is worthless.
(defn ra-split-all! [(round i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut lrg) 1
        (mut count) 0]
    (loop (if (> (load lrg) (ra-lrg-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (if (and (= (ra-find! (load lrg)) (load lrg)) (ra-lrg-failed? (load lrg)))
                    (if (ra-split-one! round (load lrg))
                        (set! (mut count) (+ (load count) 1))
                        0)
                    0)
                (set! (mut lrg) (+ (load lrg) 1))
                (continue))))
    (if (> (load count) 0) (sched-run!) 0)
    (load count)))

(defn ra-self-conflict-key [(lrg i64) (nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (+ (* (ra-find! lrg) (.self-conflict-base (ra-state))) nid))

(defn ra-self-conflict-node? [(lrg i64) (n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (hm-contains? (.self-conflicts (ra-state)) (ra-self-conflict-key lrg (n-nid n))))

(defn ra-lrg-has-self-conflict? [(lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [nids (.self-conflict-nids (ra-state))
        (mut i) 0
        (mut found) false]
    (loop (if (or (>= (load i) (len nids)) (load found))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get nids (load i)))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (ra-self-conflict-node? lrg n) (set! (mut found) true) 0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load found)))

(defn ra-self-conflict-use-visits [] (-> i64)
  (.self-conflict-use-visits (ra-state)))

(defn ra-self-conflict-sift-down! [(values (mut (ArrayList i64)))
                                   (start i64)
                                   (end i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut root) start
        (mut done) false]
    (loop (if (load done)
              (break 0)
              (let [left (+ (* (load root) 2) 1)]
                (if (>= left end)
                    (set! (mut done) true)
                    (let [(mut largest) (load root)
                          right (+ left 1)]
                      (if (< (get (load values) (load largest)) (get (load values) left))
                          (set! (mut largest) left)
                          0)
                      (if (and (< right end)
                               (< (get (load values) (load largest))
                                  (get (load values) right)))
                          (set! (mut largest) right)
                          0)
                      (if (= (load largest) (load root))
                          (set! (mut done) true)
                          (let [tmp (get (load values) (load root))]
                            (set! (mut values)
                                  (load root)
                                  (get (load values) (load largest)))
                            (set! (mut values) (load largest) tmp)
                            (set! (mut root) (load largest))))))
                (continue))))
    0))

;; Heap sort keeps the deterministic nid order final Simple obtains from Arrays.sort, without
;; turning a pathological function with many self-conflicts into quadratic compiler work.
(defn ra-sort-self-conflicts! [(values (mut (ArrayList i64)))] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut start) (- (/ (len (load values)) 2) 1)]
    (loop (if (< (load start) 0)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (ra-self-conflict-sift-down! (mut values) (load start) (len (load values)))
                (set! (mut start) (- (load start) 1))
                (continue))))
    (let [(mut end) (- (len (load values)) 1)]
      (loop (if (<= (load end) 0)
                (break 0)
                (let [tmp (get (load values) 0)]
                  (set! (mut values) 0 (get (load values) (load end)))
                  (set! (mut values) (load end) tmp)
                  (ra-self-conflict-sift-down! (mut values) 0 (load end))
                  (set! (mut end) (- (load end) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    0))

;; Simple snapshots and nid-sorts the self-conflict set before graph surgery. Keep the same
;; deterministic contract while walking only the sparse conflict index, not every arena slot.
(defn ra-self-conflicts-for [(lrg i64)] (-> (ArrayList i64))
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut conflicts) (al-new [i64] a)
        nids (.self-conflict-nids (ra-state))
        (mut i) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) (len nids))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get nids (load i)))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (ra-self-conflict-node? lrg n)
                            (push! [i64] (mut conflicts) (n-nid n))
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (ra-sort-self-conflicts! (mut conflicts))
    (load conflicts)))

(defn ra-phi? [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (match (mach-of n)
    (Some [mach] (= (m-ideal-op mach) OP-PHI))
    (None [] false)))

(defn ra-ideal-op [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (match (mach-of n) (Some [mach] (m-ideal-op mach)) (None [] (n-op n))))

(defn ra-loop-phi? [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (and (ra-phi? n) (> (n-nins n) 0) (= (ra-ideal-op (n-in! n 0)) OP-LOOP)))

(defn ra-two-address-input [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (match (mach-of n) (Some [mach] (m-two-address mach)) (None [] 0)))

;; Pre-color form of Simple's sameBlockNoClobber. A single adjacent Split already provides the
;; needed boundary when its source location is not overwritten between definition and copy.
(defn ra-same-block-no-clobber? [(split (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (if (or (!= (n-op split) OP-MACH-SPLIT) (<= (n-nins split) 1))
      false
      (let [def (n-in! split 1)
            block (ra-ifg-block-of split)]
        (if (!= (n-block-nid def) (n-nid block))
            false
            (let [def-head-nid
                    (if (and (= (ra-ideal-op def) OP-PROJ) (> (n-nins def) 0))
                        (n-nid (n-in! def 0))
                        (n-nid def))
                  def-lrg (ra-lrg-of! def)
                  assigned (if (= def-lrg 0) -1 (n-reg def))
                  defreg
                    (if (>= assigned 0)
                        assigned
                        (if (= def-lrg 0)
                            -1
                            (match (ra-lrg-mask def-lrg)
                              (Some [mask]
                                    (if (mask-empty? mask) -1 (mask-first mask)))
                              (None [] -1))))
                  (mut i) (- (ra-block-schedule-index block (n-nid split)) 1)
                  (mut clear) (>= defreg 0)
                  (mut found) false]
              (loop (if (or (< (load i) 0) (not (load clear)) (load found))
                        (break 0)
                        (let [n (code-schedule-at block (load i))]
                          (if (= (n-nid n) def-head-nid)
                              (set! (mut found) true)
                              (if (or (and (!= (ra-lrg-of! n) 0)
                                           (= (ra-lrg-of! n) def-lrg))
                                      (= (n-reg n) defreg))
                                  (set! (mut clear) false)
                                  0))
                          (set! (mut i) (- (load i) 1))
                          (continue))))
              (and (load clear) (load found)))))))

(defn ra-unique-block-successor [(block (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (let [(mut i) (- (code-schedule-count block) 1)
        (mut tail) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
        (mut successor) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
        (mut many) false]
    (loop (if (or (< (load i) 0)
                  (match (load tail) (Some [_] true) (None [] false)))
              (break 0)
              (let [n (code-schedule-at block (load i))]
                (if (cfg? n) (set! (mut tail) (Some n)) 0)
                (set! (mut i) (- (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (match (load tail)
      (None [] (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
      (Some [tail-node]
            (do
              (set! (mut i) 0)
              (loop (if (or (>= (load i) (n-nouts tail-node)) (load many))
                        (break 0)
                        (do
                          (match (n-out tail-node (load i))
                            (Some [use_]
                                  (if (cfg? use_)
                                      (match (load successor)
                                        (None [] (set! (mut successor) (Some use_)))
                                        (Some [prior]
                                              (if (n-same? prior use_)
                                                  0
                                                  (set! (mut many) true))))
                                      0))
                            (None [] 0))
                          (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                          (continue))))
              (if (load many) (None [(dyn NodeOps)]) (load successor)))))))

;; If a shallow block falls directly into a Loop and the candidate sits in its clone/Split-only
;; tail, splitting around the nominal shallow depth buys nothing. Final Simple treats that tail as
;; part of the loop; this prevents the allocator from repeatedly cutting the same loop entry.
(defn ra-split-effective-depth [(n (dyn NodeOps))
                                (block (dyn NodeOps))
                                (current-min i64)] (-> i64)
  (let [depth (looptree-depth-of block)]
    (if (>= depth current-min)
        depth
        (match (ra-unique-block-successor block)
          (Some [successor]
                (if (and (= (ra-ideal-op successor) OP-LOOP)
                         (> (n-nins successor) 1)
                         (= (n-block-nid (n-in! successor 1)) (n-nid block)))
                    (let [(mut i) (- (code-schedule-count block) 2)
                          (mut answer) depth
                          loop-depth (looptree-depth-of successor)]
                      (loop (if (< (load i) 0)
                                (break 0)
                                (let [out (code-schedule-at block (load i))]
                                  (if (n-same? out n)
                                      (do (set! (mut answer) loop-depth) (break 0))
                                      (if (or (= (n-op out) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                                              (match (mach-of out)
                                                (Some [mach] (m-clone-cheap? mach))
                                                (None [] false)))
                                          0
                                          (break 0)))
                                  (set! (mut i) (- (load i) 1))
                                  (continue))))
                      (load answer))
                    depth))
          (None [] depth)))))

;; Spill a selected CalleeSave exactly around its useful body lifetime. Final Simple's generic
;; splitByLoop reaches the same shape for a whole-function save range: one split immediately after
;; the fixed entry definition and one immediately before each boundary use, normally Return. The
;; middle range is then free to occupy a stack slot while another live range uses the callee-save
;; register across calls.
(defn ra-snapshot-register-use! [(def (dyn NodeOps))
                                 (use_ (dyn NodeOps))
                                 (uses (mut (ArrayList i64)))
                                 (indices (mut (ArrayList i64)))
                                 (seen (mut (HashMap i64 bool)))] (-> i64)
  (if (hm-contains? (load seen) (n-nid use_))
      0
      (do
        (set! (mut seen) (n-nid use_) true)
        (match (mach-of use_)
          (Some [mach]
                (let [(mut idx) 1]
                  (loop (if (>= (load idx) (n-nins use_))
                            (break 0)
                            (do
                              (match (n-in use_ (load idx))
                                (Some [input]
                                      (if (n-same? input def)
                                          (match (m-regmap mach (load idx))
                                            (Some [_]
                                                  (do
                                                    (push! [i64] (mut uses) (n-nid use_))
                                                    (push! [i64] (mut indices) (load idx))))
                                            (None [] 0))
                                          0))
                                (None [] 0))
                              (set! (mut idx) (+ (load idx) 1))
                              (continue))))))
          (None [] 0)))))

(defn ra-split-callee-save! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
        a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut uses) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut indices) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut seen-uses) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a)
        def-nid (get (.callee-save-defs (ra-state)) leader)
        (mut oi) 0]
    (if (= def-nid 0)
        false
        (match (arena-node def-nid)
          (None []
                (do
                  (panic "ra-split-callee-save!: saved definition disappeared")
                  false))
          (Some [def]
                (do
                  ;; Snapshot direct register-bearing uses before the entry split rewires them.
                  ;; The definition's outputs are the sparse authoritative use index.
                  (set! (mut oi) 0)
                  (loop (if (>= (load oi) (n-nouts def))
                            (break 0)
                            (do
                              (match (n-out def (load oi))
                                (Some [use_]
                                      (ra-snapshot-register-use! def
                                                                 use_
                                                                 (mut uses)
                                                                 (mut indices)
                                                                 (mut seen-uses)))
                                (None [] 0))
                              (set! (mut oi) (+ (load oi) 1))
                              (continue))))
                  (ra-split-after-def-node! round leader def SPLIT-KIND-AFTER-DEF)
                  (let [(mut i) 0]
                    (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (load uses)))
                              (break 0)
                              (do
                                (match (arena-node (get (load uses) (load i)))
                                  (Some [use_]
                                        (do
                                          (ra-split-before-use-node! round
                                                                     leader
                                                                     use_
                                                                     (get (load indices) (load i))
                                                                     SPLIT-KIND-BEFORE-USE)
                                          0))
                                  (None []
                                        (do
                                          (panic "ra-split-callee-save!: boundary use disappeared")
                                          0)))
                                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                                (continue)))))
                  true))))))

;; Final Simple's `findAllLRG` starts from one representative def/use and expands through same-LRG
;; inputs plus every output use. Failed-range splitting is therefore proportional to that range's
;; def-use component, not to the complete compilation arena.
(defn ra-lrg-member-push! [(members (mut (ArrayList i64)))
                           (seen (mut (HashMap i64 bool)))
                           (nid i64)] (-> i64)
  (if (or (<= nid 0) (hm-contains? (load seen) nid))
      0
      (match (arena-node nid)
        (Some [n]
              (if (n-dead? n)
                  0
                  (do
                    (set! (mut seen) nid true)
                    (push! [i64] (mut members) nid))))
        (None [] 0))))

(defn ra-find-all-lrg [(lrg i64)] (-> (ArrayList i64))
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! lrg)
        (mut members) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut seen) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a)
        (mut index) 0]
    (ra-lrg-member-push! (mut members) (mut seen) (get (.mach-defs state) leader))
    (ra-lrg-member-push! (mut members) (mut seen) (get (.mach-uses state) leader))
    (ra-lrg-member-push! (mut members) (mut seen) (get (.split-defs state) leader))
    (ra-lrg-member-push! (mut members) (mut seen) (get (.split-uses state) leader))
    (loop (if (>= (load index) (len (load members)))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get (load members) (load index)))
                  (Some [n]
                        (do
                          ;; A representative machine use need not itself define this LRG. Always
                          ;; cross its matching input edges so input-only global/rematerializable
                          ;; definitions enter the component. Output expansion, by contrast, is
                          ;; meaningful only for a node that actually defines the range.
                          (let [(mut ii) 0]
                            (loop (if (>= (load ii) (n-nins n))
                                      (break 0)
                                      (do
                                        (match (n-in n (load ii))
                                          (Some [def]
                                                (if (= (ra-lrg-of! def) leader)
                                                    (ra-lrg-member-push! (mut members)
                                                                         (mut seen)
                                                                         (n-nid def))
                                                    0))
                                          (None [] 0))
                                        (set! (mut ii) (+ (load ii) 1))
                                        (continue)))))
                          (if (= (ra-lrg-of! n) leader)
                              (let [(mut oi) 0]
                                (loop (if (>= (load oi) (n-nouts n))
                                          (break 0)
                                          (do
                                            (match (n-out n (load oi))
                                              (Some [use_]
                                                    (ra-lrg-member-push! (mut members)
                                                                         (mut seen)
                                                                         (n-nid use_)))
                                              (None [] 0))
                                            (set! (mut oi) (+ (load oi) 1))
                                            (continue)))))
                              0)))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut index) (+ (load index) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load members)))

;; Final Simple's generic `splitByLoop` cuts BOTH sides of the selected loop boundary: after defs
;; to leave a broad spillable middle range, and before uses to isolate their narrower register
;; constraints. Merely replacing Split(def) with another Split(def) cannot repair an IFG failure
;; caused by a finite Call-use range overlapping Return's fixed callee-save uses.
(defn ra-split-by-loop-boundary! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
        a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut defs) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut def-depths) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut uses) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut indices) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut use-depths) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut min-depth) 9999
        (mut max-depth) -1
        members (ra-find-all-lrg leader)
        (mut member-index) 0]
    ;; Snapshot before mutation, as Simple snapshots `_ns`. Split nodes remain candidates when all
    ;; defs and uses are at one depth, but do not themselves define the min/max loop boundary.
    (loop (if (>= (load member-index) (len members))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get members (load member-index)))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (n-dead? n)
                            0
                            (match (mach-of n)
                              (Some [mach]
                                    (do
                                      ;; Final Simple commutes a two-address def when the RHS has
                                      ;; one use. The overwritten input then dies at this op instead
                                      ;; of forcing the failed LRG to span the RHS computation.
                                      (if (and (= (ra-lrg-of! n) leader)
                                               (= (m-two-address mach) 1)
                                               (m-commutes mach)
                                               (> (n-nins n) 2)
                                               (= (n-nouts (n-in! n 2)) 1))
                                          (do (n-swap12! n) 0)
                                          0)
                                      (if (and (= (ra-lrg-of! n) leader)
                                               (match (m-outregmap mach)
                                                 (Some [_] true)
                                                 (None [] false)))
                                          (let [def-block (ra-ifg-block-of n)
                                                depth
                                                  (ra-split-effective-depth n
                                                                            def-block
                                                                            (load min-depth))]
                                            (push! [i64] (mut defs) (n-nid n))
                                            (push! [i64] (mut def-depths) depth)
                                            (if (!= (n-op n) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                                                (do
                                                  (if (< depth (load min-depth))
                                                      (set! (mut min-depth) depth)
                                                      0)
                                                  (if (> depth (load max-depth))
                                                      (set! (mut max-depth) depth)
                                                      0))
                                                0))
                                          0)
                                      (let [(mut idx) 1]
                                        (loop (if (>= (load idx) (n-nins n))
                                                  (break 0)
                                                  (do
                                                    (match (n-in n (load idx))
                                                      (Some [input]
                                                            (if (= (ra-lrg-of! input) leader)
                                                                (match (m-regmap mach (load idx))
                                                                  (Some [_]
                                                                        (let [use-block
                                                                                (ra-split-block-for-use n
                                                                                                        (load idx))
                                                                              depth
                                                                                (ra-split-effective-depth input
                                                                                                          use-block
                                                                                                          (load min-depth))
                                                                              count-depth
                                                                                (if (ra-phi? n)
                                                                                    (!= (n-op input)
                                                                                        OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                                                                                    (!= (n-op n)
                                                                                        OP-MACH-SPLIT))]
                                                                          (push! [i64]
                                                                                 (mut uses)
                                                                                 (n-nid n))
                                                                          (push! [i64]
                                                                                 (mut indices)
                                                                                 (load idx))
                                                                          (push! [i64]
                                                                                 (mut use-depths)
                                                                                 depth)
                                                                          (if count-depth
                                                                              (do
                                                                                (if (< depth
                                                                                       (load min-depth))
                                                                                    (set! (mut min-depth)
                                                                                          depth)
                                                                                    0)
                                                                                (if (> depth
                                                                                       (load max-depth))
                                                                                    (set! (mut max-depth)
                                                                                          depth)
                                                                                    0))
                                                                              0)))
                                                                  (None [] 0))
                                                                0))
                                                      (None [] 0))
                                                    (set! (mut idx) (+ (load idx) 1))
                                                    (continue)))))
                                      0))
                              (None [] 0))))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut member-index) (+ (load member-index) 1))
                (continue))))
    (if (= (load max-depth) -1)
        false
        (let [state (ra-state)
              fixed-defs (get (.fixed-def-counts state) leader)
              fixed-uses (get (.fixed-use-counts state) leader)
              empty-multi
                (and (match (ra-lrg-mask leader)
                       (Some [mask] (mask-empty? mask))
                       (None [] false))
                     (and (get (.multi-defs state) leader)
                          (and (<= fixed-defs 1)
                               (or (> fixed-uses 1)
                                   (> (+ (len (load defs)) (len (load uses))) 5)))))
              (mut changed) false
              (mut i) 0]
          ;; Ordinary pressure splits choose the shallow side of the outermost loop boundary. The
          ;; multi-definition hot-side exception remains handled by the fixed-def path above.
          (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (load defs)))
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (match (arena-node (get (load defs) (load i)))
                        (Some [def]
                              (if (and (not (n-dead? def))
                                       (or (= (load min-depth) (load max-depth))
                                           (if empty-multi
                                               (>= (get (load def-depths) (load i))
                                                   (load max-depth))
                                               (<= (get (load def-depths) (load i))
                                                   (load min-depth)))))
                                  (match (mach-of def)
                                    (Some [mach]
                                          (if (and (not (m-clone-cheap? mach))
                                                   (not (and (= (n-nouts def) 1)
                                                             (match (n-out def 0)
                                                               (Some [out]
                                                                     (and (= (n-op out)
                                                                             OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                                                                          (ra-same-block-no-clobber? out)))
                                                               (None [] false)))))
                                              (do
                                                (ra-split-after-def-node! round
                                                                          leader
                                                                          def
                                                                          SPLIT-KIND-AFTER-DEF)
                                                (set! (mut changed) true))
                                              0))
                                    (None [] 0))
                                  0))
                        (None [] 0))
                      (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                      (continue))))
          (set! (mut i) 0)
          (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (load uses)))
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (match (arena-node (get (load uses) (load i)))
                        (Some [use_]
                              (let [idx (get (load indices) (load i))]
                                (if (and (not (n-dead? use_))
                                         (< idx (n-nins use_))
                                         (and (match (n-in use_ idx)
                                                (Some [_] true)
                                                (None [] false))
                                              (or (= (load min-depth) (load max-depth))
                                                  (match (mach-of (n-in! use_ idx))
                                                    (Some [input-mach]
                                                          (m-clone-cheap? input-mach))
                                                    (None [] false))
                                                  (if empty-multi
                                                      (>= (get (load use-depths) (load i))
                                                          (load max-depth))
                                                      (<= (get (load use-depths) (load i))
                                                          (load min-depth))))))
                                    ;; Generic ordinary uses deliberately pass skip=false, exactly
                                    ;; as Simple does, so a use-side cut is not bypassed back to the
                                    ;; failing same-block Split. Phi edges retain the safe bypass.
                                    (if (or (and (ra-phi? use_)
                                                 (= (n-op (n-in! use_ idx)) OP-MACH-SPLIT))
                                            ;; Do not force a Split around a loop's own carried-Phi
                                            ;; backedge; it is hot and especially hard to remove.
                                            (and (ra-loop-phi? use_)
                                                 (= idx 2)
                                                 (let [input (n-in! use_ idx)]
                                                   (and (ra-phi? input)
                                                        (n-same? (n-in! input 0)
                                                                 (n-in! use_ 0))))))
                                        0
                                        (do
                                          (ra-split-before-use-node-mode! round
                                                                          leader
                                                                          use_
                                                                          idx
                                                                          SPLIT-KIND-BEFORE-USE
                                                                          (ra-phi? use_))
                                          (set! (mut changed) true)))
                                    0)))
                        (None [] 0))
                      (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                      (continue))))
          (load changed)))))

(defn ra-lrg-mask-empty? [(lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (match (ra-lrg-mask lrg) (Some [mask] (mask-empty? mask)) (None [] true)))

;; Final Simple's cheap empty-mask case: isolate the one fixed definition and/or one fixed use
;; directly, without surrounding every constrained endpoint in the LRG.
(defn ra-split-empty-simple! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! lrg)
        fixed-defs (get (.fixed-def-counts state) leader)
        fixed-uses (get (.fixed-use-counts state) leader)
        def-id (get (.mach-defs state) leader)
        use-id (get (.mach-uses state) leader)
        (mut changed) false
        (mut def-outs) 0]
    (if (ra-trace?)
        (do (println "ra:   empty-simple: def {} use {} fixed-defs {} fixed-uses {} def-clone-cheap {}"
                     def-id use-id fixed-defs fixed-uses
                     (match (arena-node def-id)
                       (Some [def] (match (mach-of def) (Some [mach] (if (m-clone-cheap? mach) 1 0)) (None [] -1)))
                       (None [] -2)))
            0)
        0)
    (if (!= def-id 0)
        (match (arena-node def-id)
          (Some [def]
                (do
                  (set! (mut def-outs) (n-nouts def))
                  (if (= fixed-defs 1)
                      (match (mach-of def)
                        (Some [mach]
                              (if (not (m-clone-cheap? mach))
                                  (do
                                    (ra-split-after-def-node! round
                                                              leader
                                                              def
                                                              SPLIT-KIND-AFTER-DEF)
                                    (set! (mut changed) true))
                                  0))
                        (None [] 0))
                      0)))
          (None [] 0))
        0)
    (if (and (!= use-id 0)
             (or (= fixed-uses 1) (and (= fixed-defs 1) (= (load def-outs) 1))))
        (match (arena-node use-id)
          (Some [use_]
                (let [idx (get (.mach-use-inputs state) leader)]
                  (if (and (> idx 0) (< idx (n-nins use_)))
                      (do
                        (ra-split-before-use-node! round
                                                   leader
                                                   use_
                                                   idx
                                                   SPLIT-KIND-BEFORE-USE)
                        (set! (mut changed) true))
                      0)))
          (None [] 0))
        0)
    (load changed)))

;; Several fixed uses on a multi-definition empty LRG are split directly only when the range is
;; genuinely broad. This is Simple's emptyN guard; on small ranges the generic loop boundary gives
;; fewer moves.
(defn ra-lrg-member-count [(lrg i64)] (-> i64)
  (len (ra-find-all-lrg lrg)))

(defn ra-split-empty-single-uses! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
        members (ra-find-all-lrg leader)
        (mut member-index) 0
        (mut changed) false]
    (if (<= (len members) 5)
        false
        (do
          (loop (if (>= (load member-index) (len members))
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (match (arena-node (get members (load member-index)))
                        (Some [use_]
                              (match (mach-of use_)
                                (Some [mach]
                                      (let [(mut idx) 1]
                                        (loop (if (>= (load idx) (n-nins use_))
                                                  (break 0)
                                                  (do
                                                    (match (n-in use_ (load idx))
                                                      (Some [def]
                                                            (if (= (ra-lrg-of! def) leader)
                                                                (match (m-regmap mach (load idx))
                                                                  (Some [mask]
                                                                        (if (mask-singleton? mask)
                                                                            (do
                                                                              (ra-split-before-use-node! round
                                                                                                         leader
                                                                                                         use_
                                                                                                         (load idx)
                                                                                                         SPLIT-KIND-BEFORE-USE)
                                                                              (set! (mut changed)
                                                                                    true))
                                                                            0))
                                                                  (None [] 0))
                                                                0))
                                                      (None [] 0))
                                                    (set! (mut idx) (+ (load idx) 1))
                                                    (continue))))))
                                (None [] 0)))
                        (None [] 0))
                      (set! (mut member-index) (+ (load member-index) 1))
                      (continue))))
          (load changed)))))

(defn ra-mask-subset? [(left (ptr RegMask)) (right (ptr RegMask))] (-> bool)
  (mask-empty? (mask-sub left right)))

;; A single-def range with many fixed uses is partitioned into overlapping register classes, as in
;; final Simple's `splitEmptyMaskByUse`. One Split serves every use in a class instead of emitting a
;; private copy at every call/ABI use; more than one Call declines because caller-save kills dominate
;; the benefit.
(defn ra-split-empty-by-use-class! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! lrg)
        def-id (get (.mach-defs state) leader)
        (mut uses) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut indices) (al-new [i64] a)
        (mut masks) (al-new [(ptr RegMask)] a)
        (mut classes) (al-new [(ptr RegMask)] a)
        (mut calls) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a)
        (mut oi) 0]
    (if (= def-id 0)
        false
        (match (arena-node def-id)
          (None [] false)
          (Some [def]
                (do
                  ;; The representative def's sparse outputs are authoritative in this single-def
                  ;; case; do not rescan the arena for every failing LRG.
                  (loop (if (>= (load oi) (n-nouts def))
                            (break 0)
                            (do
                              (match (n-out def (load oi))
                                (Some [use_]
                                      (match (mach-of use_)
                                        (Some [mach]
                                              (let [(mut idx) 1]
                                                (loop (if (>= (load idx) (n-nins use_))
                                                          (break 0)
                                                          (do
                                                            (match (n-in use_ (load idx))
                                                              (Some [input]
                                                                    (if (n-same? input def)
                                                                        (match (m-regmap mach (load idx))
                                                                          (Some [mask]
                                                                                (do
                                                                                  (push! [i64]
                                                                                         (mut uses)
                                                                                         (n-nid use_))
                                                                                  (push! [i64]
                                                                                         (mut indices)
                                                                                         (load idx))
                                                                                  (push! [(ptr RegMask)]
                                                                                         (mut masks)
                                                                                         mask)
                                                                                  (if (= (m-ideal-op mach)
                                                                                         OP-CALL)
                                                                                      (set! (mut calls)
                                                                                            (n-nid use_)
                                                                                            true)
                                                                                      0)))
                                                                          (None [] 0))
                                                                        0))
                                                              (None [] 0))
                                                            (set! (mut idx) (+ (load idx) 1))
                                                            (continue))))))
                                        (None [] 0)))
                                (None [] 0))
                              (set! (mut oi) (+ (load oi) 1))
                              (continue))))
                  (let [(mut stable) false]
                    (loop (if (load stable)
                              (break 0)
                              (do
                                (set! (mut stable) true)
                                (let [(mut mi) 0]
                                  (loop (if (>= (load mi) (len (load masks)))
                                            (break 0)
                                            (let [mask (get (load masks) (load mi))
                                                  (mut ci) 0
                                                  (mut placed) false]
                                              (loop (if (or (>= (load ci) (len (load classes)))
                                                            (load placed))
                                                        (break 0)
                                                        (let [old (get (load classes) (load ci))]
                                                          (if (ra-mask-subset? old mask)
                                                              (set! (mut placed) true)
                                                              (if (mask-overlap? old mask)
                                                                  (do
                                                                    (set! (mut classes)
                                                                          (load ci)
                                                                          (mask-and old mask))
                                                                    (set! (mut placed) true)
                                                                    (set! (mut stable) false))
                                                                  0))
                                                          (set! (mut ci) (+ (load ci) 1))
                                                          (continue))))
                                              (if (not (load placed))
                                                  (push! [(ptr RegMask)] (mut classes) mask)
                                                  0)
                                              (set! (mut mi) (+ (load mi) 1))
                                              (continue)))))
                                (continue)))))
                  (if (or (<= (len (load classes)) 1) (> (len (load calls)) 1))
                      false
                      (let [(mut ci) 0
                            (mut changed) false]
                        (loop (if (>= (load ci) (len (load classes)))
                                  (break 0)
                                  (let [class (get (load classes) (load ci))
                                        split
                                          (mach-make-split leader
                                                           SPLIT-KIND-AFTER-DEF
                                                           round
                                                           (ra-ifg-block-of def)
                                                           def)
                                        (mut ui) 0
                                        (mut rewired) 0]
                                    (ra-place-copy! split (ra-ifg-block-of def))
                                    (loop (if (>= (load ui) (len (load uses)))
                                              (break 0)
                                              (do
                                                (match (arena-node (get (load uses) (load ui)))
                                                  (Some [use_]
                                                        (let [idx (get (load indices) (load ui))]
                                                          (if (and (< idx (n-nins use_))
                                                                   (match (n-in use_ idx)
                                                                     (Some [input]
                                                                           (n-same? input def))
                                                                     (None [] false))
                                                                   (mask-overlap? (get (load masks) (load ui))
                                                                                  class))
                                                              (do
                                                                (n-set-def! use_ idx (Some split))
                                                                (set! (mut rewired)
                                                                      (+ (load rewired) 1)))
                                                              0)))
                                                  (None [] 0))
                                                (set! (mut ui) (+ (load ui) 1))
                                                (continue))))
                                    (if (= (load rewired) 0)
                                        (n-kill! split)
                                        (set! (mut changed) true))
                                    (set! (mut ci) (+ (load ci) 1))
                                    (continue))))
                        (load changed)))))))))

(defn ra-split-managed-root-def! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  ;; Phi coalescing may join a managed loop value, whose legal GC home is a stack slot, to a
  ;; register-only producer such as Box or Load. Split exactly one such producer per allocation
  ;; round. The Phi remains in the rooted stack range while the producer gets the ordinary broad
  ;; input side of an after-definition copy. This is the definition-side counterpart to the
  ;; register-only consumer boundary below.
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
        members (ra-find-all-lrg leader)
        roots (selected-gc-root-mask)
        (mut mi) 0
        (mut found) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load mi) (len members))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get members (load mi)))
                  (Some [def]
                        (if (and (not (ra-phi? def))
                                 (and (> (ra-lrg-of! def) 0)
                                      (= (ra-find! (ra-lrg-of! def)) leader)))
                            (match (mach-of def)
                              (Some [mach]
                                    (match (m-outregmap mach)
                                      (Some [produced]
                                            (if (not (mask-overlap? roots produced))
                                                (do
                                                  (set! (mut found) (n-nid def))
                                                  (break 0))
                                                0))
                                      (None [] 0)))
                              (None [] 0))
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut mi) (+ (load mi) 1))
                (continue))))
    (if (= (load found) 0)
        false
        (match (arena-node (load found))
          (Some [def]
                (do
                  (ra-split-after-def-node! round leader def SPLIT-KIND-AFTER-DEF)
                  true))
          (None []
                (do
                  (panic "ra-split-managed-root-def!: selected definition disappeared")
                  false))))))

(defn ra-split-managed-root-uses! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  ;; A managed value live across Call/New is intentionally restricted to the target's addressable
  ;; root homes. A later register-only consumer therefore needs a reload boundary; treating this
  ;; as ordinary pressure and splitting the definition side merely reproduces the empty range.
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
        members (ra-find-all-lrg leader)
        roots (selected-gc-root-mask)
        (mut mi) 0
        (mut changed) false]
    (loop (if (>= (load mi) (len members))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get members (load mi)))
                  (Some [use_]
                        (match (mach-of use_)
                          (Some [mach]
                                (let [(mut idx) 1]
                                  (loop (if (>= (load idx) (n-nins use_))
                                            (break 0)
                                            (do
                                              (match (n-in use_ (load idx))
                                                (Some [value]
                                                      (if (and (> (ra-lrg-of! value) 0)
                                                               (= (ra-find! (ra-lrg-of! value))
                                                                  leader))
                                                          (match (m-regmap mach (load idx))
                                                            (Some [required]
                                                                  (if (not (mask-overlap? roots required))
                                                                      (do
                                                                        (ra-split-before-use-node! round
                                                                                                   leader
                                                                                                   use_
                                                                                                   (load idx)
                                                                                                   SPLIT-KIND-BEFORE-USE)
                                                                        (set! (mut changed) true))
                                                                      0))
                                                            (None [] 0))
                                                          0))
                                                (None [] 0))
                                              (set! (mut idx) (+ (load idx) 1))
                                              (continue))))))
                          (None [] 0)))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut mi) (+ (load mi) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load changed)))

(defn ra-split-pressure-use! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  ;; A range can fail coloring because its interference clique consumes every allowed color even
  ;; when no loop-depth boundary distinguishes a cheaper side. Snapshot-based splitting permits
  ;; every ordinary use boundary to be cut in the same retry, as Simple's splitLRG does after it
  ;; has selected the failed range.
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
        members (ra-find-all-lrg leader)
        (mut mi) 0
        (mut changed) false]
    (loop (if (>= (load mi) (len members))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get members (load mi)))
                  (Some [use_]
                        (match (mach-of use_)
                          (Some [mach]
                                (let [(mut idx) 1]
                                  (loop (if (>= (load idx) (n-nins use_))
                                            (break 0)
                                            (do
                                              (match (n-in use_ (load idx))
                                                (Some [input]
                                                      (if (and (> (ra-lrg-of! input) 0)
                                                               (= (ra-find! (ra-lrg-of! input))
                                                                  leader))
                                                          (match (m-regmap mach (load idx))
                                                            (Some [_]
                                                                  (do
                                                                    (ra-split-before-use-node! round
                                                                                               leader
                                                                                               use_
                                                                                               (load idx)
                                                                                               SPLIT-KIND-BEFORE-USE)
                                                                    (set! (mut changed) true)))
                                                            (None [] 0))
                                                          0))
                                                (None [] 0))
                                              (set! (mut idx) (+ (load idx) 1))
                                              (continue))))))
                          (None [] 0)))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut mi) (+ (load mi) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load changed)))

(defn ra-split-one! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (do
    (if (ra-trace?) (do (println "ra: split lrg {}" (ra-find! lrg)) 0) 0)
    (ra-split-one-policy! round lrg)))

(defn ra-trace-policy! [(what (slice u8))] (-> i64)
  (if (ra-trace?) (do (println "ra:   policy {s}" what) 0) 0))

(defn ra-split-one-policy! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (if (ra-lrg-has-self-conflict? lrg)
      (do (ra-trace-policy! "self-conflict") (ra-split-self-conflict! round lrg))
      (if (ra-lrg-has-callee-save-def? lrg)
          (do (ra-trace-policy! "callee-save") (ra-split-callee-save! round lrg))
          (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
                state (ra-state)
                fixed-defs (get (.fixed-def-counts state) leader)
                fixed-uses (get (.fixed-use-counts state) leader)
                empty (ra-lrg-mask-empty? leader)]
            (if (and empty
                     (!= (ra-lrg-kind leader) LRG-SCALAR)
                     (get (.root-restricted state) leader)
                     (or (do (ra-trace-policy! "managed-root-def") (ra-split-managed-root-def! round leader))
                         (do (ra-trace-policy! "managed-root-uses") (ra-split-managed-root-uses! round leader))))
                true
                (if (and empty (<= fixed-defs 1) (<= fixed-uses 1) (> (+ fixed-defs fixed-uses) 0))
                    ;; Simple's empty1 returns true even when a cloneable fixed def with multiple
                    ;; uses causes both insertion guards to skip. A shared XZR constant joined to
                    ;; nonconstant Phi arms reaches that case here. Only claim the cheap split
                    ;; when it changed an edge; otherwise use the ordinary boundary splitter.
                    (if (do (ra-trace-policy! "empty-simple") (ra-split-empty-simple! round leader))
                        true
                        (do (ra-trace-policy! "loop-boundary (after empty-simple)")
                            (ra-split-by-loop-boundary! round leader)))
                    (if (and empty (not (get (.multi-defs state) leader)) (<= fixed-defs 1) (> fixed-uses 1))
                        (if (do (ra-trace-policy! "empty-by-use-class") (ra-split-empty-by-use-class! round leader))
                            true
                            (do (ra-trace-policy! "loop-boundary (after use-class)")
                                (ra-split-by-loop-boundary! round leader)))
                        (if (and empty (get (.multi-defs state) leader) (> fixed-uses 1) (<= fixed-defs 1))
                            (if (do (ra-trace-policy! "empty-single-uses") (ra-split-empty-single-uses! round leader))
                                true
                                (do (ra-trace-policy! "loop-boundary (after single-uses)")
                                    (ra-split-by-loop-boundary! round leader)))
                            (if (do (ra-trace-policy! "fixed-neighbour-defs") (ra-split-fixed-neighbour-defs! round leader))
                                true
                                (if (do (ra-trace-policy! "loop-boundary") (ra-split-by-loop-boundary! round leader))
                                    true
                                    (do (ra-trace-policy! "pressure-use")
                                        (ra-split-pressure-use! round leader))))))))))))

;; A range whose only allowed register is R fails while a neighbour BORN in R — a fixed
;; single-register definition such as an allocation or call result in X0 — still holds R at our
;; definition (its last use, a copy into another argument register, comes after ours). Copies of
;; our own range cannot help; every round would re-make one. The answer is the neighbour's: split
;; it after its definition, so it leaves R at once and R is free where we need it.
(defn ra-split-fixed-neighbour-defs! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [state (ra-state)
        leader (ra-find! lrg)]
    (match (ra-lrg-mask leader)
      (None [] false)
      (Some [mask]
            (if (not (mask-singleton? mask))
                false
                (let [reg (mask-first mask)
                      (mut edge) (get (.adj-heads state) leader)
                      (mut changed) false]
                  (loop (if (< (load edge) 0)
                            (break 0)
                            (let [other (ra-find! (get (.adj-to state) (load edge)))
                                  def-id (get (.mach-defs state) other)]
                              (if (and (= (ra-lrg-reg other) reg)
                                       (!= def-id 0)
                                       (= (get (.fixed-def-counts state) other) 1))
                                  (match (arena-node def-id)
                                    (Some [def]
                                          (match (mach-of def)
                                            (Some [mach]
                                                  (if (m-clone-cheap? mach)
                                                      0
                                                      (do
                                                        (if (ra-trace?)
                                                            (do (println "ra:   splitting neighbour lrg {} after its fixed definition" other) 0)
                                                            0)
                                                        (ra-split-after-def-node! round other def SPLIT-KIND-AFTER-DEF)
                                                        (set! (mut changed) true)
                                                        0)))
                                            (None [] 0)))
                                    (None [] 0))
                                  0)
                              (set! (mut edge) (get (.adj-next state) (load edge)))
                              (continue))))
                  (load changed)))))))

;; A live range that conflicts with ITSELF — typically a Phi whose inputs need different registers.
;; Loop Phis are split cold-edges-first; see the header.
;; Final Simple's insertBefore skips an existing Split only if it is in the effective use block,
;; has that sole use, and the use is not fixed to one register. A Split after a Parm in the Fun
;; block does NOT satisfy a Phi edge in a successor block: treating every Split as sufficient
;; forces the two alternative values to be defined in the same LRG simultaneously.
(defn ra-use-split-sufficient? [(use_ (dyn NodeOps)) (idx i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [input (n-in! use_ idx)
        block (ra-split-block-for-use use_ idx)]
    (and (= (n-op input) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
         (= (n-block-nid input) (n-nid block))
         (= (n-nouts input) 1)
         (match (mach-of use_)
           (Some [mach]
             (match (m-regmap mach idx) (Some [mask] (not (mask-singleton? mask))) (None [] true)))
           (None [] true)))))

(defn ra-split-self-conflict! [(round i64) (lrg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [leader (ra-find! lrg)
        a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut defer-now) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a)
        conflicts (ra-self-conflicts-for leader)
        (mut nid) 0
        (mut count) 0]
    ;; Discover loop Phis touched by the conflict. A Phi absent from the persistent set gets one
    ;; cold-only round; seeing it again means the cold split failed and hot edges are now eligible.
    (loop (if (>= (load nid) (len conflicts))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get conflicts (load nid)))
                  (Some [def]
                        (if (ra-self-conflict-node? leader def)
                            (do
                              (if (ra-loop-phi? def)
                                  (if (not (hm-contains? (.deferred-loop-self (ra-state))
                                                         (n-nid def)))
                                      (do
                                        (set! (mut defer-now) (n-nid def) true)
                                        (set! (mut (.deferred-loop-self (ra-state)))
                                              (n-nid def)
                                              true))
                                      0)
                                  0)
                              (let [(mut use-index) 0]
                                (loop (if (>= (load use-index) (n-nouts def))
                                          (break 0)
                                          (do
                                            (set! (mut (.self-conflict-use-visits (ra-state)))
                                                  (+ (.self-conflict-use-visits (ra-state)) 1))
                                            (match (n-out def (load use-index))
                                              (Some [use_]
                                                    (if (and (ra-loop-phi? use_)
                                                             (> (n-nins use_) 2)
                                                             (n-same? (n-in! use_ 2) def)
                                                             (not (hm-contains? (.deferred-loop-self (ra-state))
                                                                                (n-nid use_))))
                                                        (do
                                                          (set! (mut defer-now)
                                                                (n-nid use_)
                                                                true)
                                                          (set! (mut (.deferred-loop-self (ra-state)))
                                                                (n-nid use_)
                                                                true))
                                                        0))
                                              (None [] 0))
                                            (set! (mut use-index) (+ (load use-index) 1))
                                            (continue)))))
                              0)
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut nid) (+ (load nid) 1))
                (continue))))
    ;; Split every conflict in nid order. Phi uses are placed in their matching predecessor block;
    ;; two-address uses are split at the instruction. Deferred loop backedges and Phi definitions
    ;; are the only hot pieces withheld on the first encounter.
    (set! (mut nid) 0)
    (loop (if (>= (load nid) (len conflicts))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (get conflicts (load nid)))
                  (Some [def]
                        (if (ra-self-conflict-node? leader def)
                            (do
                              (let [(mut use-index) 0]
                                (loop (if (>= (load use-index) (n-nouts def))
                                          (break 0)
                                          (do
                                            (set! (mut (.self-conflict-use-visits (ra-state)))
                                                  (+ (.self-conflict-use-visits (ra-state)) 1))
                                            (match (n-out def (load use-index))
                                              (Some [use_]
                                                    (let [(mut idx) 1]
                                                      (loop (if (>= (load idx) (n-nins use_))
                                                                (break 0)
                                                                (do
                                                                  (match (n-in use_ (load idx))
                                                                    (Some [input]
                                                                          (if (n-same? input def)
                                                                              (if (or (ra-phi? use_)
                                                                                      (= (ra-two-address-input use_)
                                                                                         (load idx)))
                                                                                  (if (and (ra-loop-phi? use_)
                                                                                           (= (load idx) 2)
                                                                                           (or (hm-contains? (load defer-now)
                                                                                                             (n-nid use_))
                                                                                               ;; Final Simple does not split a loop Phi's
                                                                                               ;; backedge when the definition already comes
                                                                                               ;; from deeper control inside that loop.
                                                                                               (> (cfg-idepth-of (ra-ifg-block-of def))
                                                                                                  (cfg-idepth-of (n-in! use_
                                                                                                                        0)))))
                                                                                      0
                                                                                      (if (ra-use-split-sufficient? use_ (load idx))
                                                                                          0
                                                                                          (do
                                                                                            (ra-split-before-use-node! round
                                                                                                                       leader
                                                                                                                       use_
                                                                                                                       (load idx)
                                                                                                                       SPLIT-KIND-SELF)
                                                                                            (set! (mut count)
                                                                                                  (+ (load count)
                                                                                                     1)))))
                                                                                  0)
                                                                              0))
                                                                    (None [] 0))
                                                                  (set! (mut idx) (+ (load idx) 1))
                                                                  (continue))))))
                                              (None [] 0))
                                            (set! (mut use-index) (+ (load use-index) 1))
                                            (continue)))))
                              (if (ra-phi? def)
                                  (do
                                    (if (not (hm-contains? (load defer-now) (n-nid def)))
                                        (do
                                          (ra-split-after-def-node! round
                                                                    leader
                                                                    def
                                                                    SPLIT-KIND-SELF)
                                          (set! (mut count) (+ (load count) 1)))
                                        0)
                                    (if (and (> (n-nins def) 1)
                                             (not (ra-use-split-sufficient? def 1)))
                                        (do
                                          (ra-split-before-use-node! round
                                                                     leader
                                                                     def
                                                                     1
                                                                     SPLIT-KIND-SELF)
                                          (set! (mut count) (+ (load count) 1)))
                                        0))
                                  (let [two (ra-two-address-input def)]
                                    (if (> two 0)
                                        (do
                                          (ra-split-before-use-node! round
                                                                     leader
                                                                     def
                                                                     two
                                                                     SPLIT-KIND-SELF)
                                          (set! (mut count) (+ (load count) 1)))
                                        0)))
                              0)
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut nid) (+ (load nid) 1))
                (continue))))
    (> (load count) 0)))

;; Finalize each function from its actual colored high-water mark. Stack argument locations and
;; spill locations share the allocator namespace, so this one scan accounts for both.
(defn ra-finalize-frames! [] (-> i64)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut block-owners) (hm-new-scalar [i64 i64] a)
        (mut max-locations) (hm-new-scalar [i64 i64] a)
        (mut call-functions) (hm-new-scalar [i64 bool] a)
        (mut ci) 0
        (mut nid) 1
        (mut count) 0]
    ;; Cache ownership once per CFG block. Looking it up for every node avoids the old
    ;; functions*arena nested scan and repeated dominator walks on large closed-world programs.
    (loop (if (>= (load ci) (code-cfg-count))
              (break 0)
              (let [block (code-cfg-at (load ci))]
                (match (ra-enclosing-fun block)
                  (Some [fun] (set! (mut block-owners) (n-nid block) (n-nid fun)))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut ci) (+ (load ci) 1))
                (continue))))
    (loop (if (> (load nid) (arena-node-count))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load nid))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (= (n-block-nid n) 0)
                            0
                            (match (get (load block-owners) (n-block-nid n))
                              (Some [owner]
                                    (do
                                      (if (>= (n-reg n) 0)
                                          (let [top (+ (n-reg n) 1)
                                                prior
                                                  (match (get (load max-locations) owner)
                                                    (Some [value] value)
                                                    (None [] 0))]
                                            (if (> top prior)
                                                (set! (mut max-locations) owner top)
                                                0))
                                          0)
                                      (let [op (ra-ideal-op n)]
                                        (if (or (= op OP-CALL)
                                                (= op OP-CALLEND)
                                                (= op OP-NEW)
                                                (= op OP-JSOP))
                                            (set! (mut call-functions) owner true)
                                            0))))
                              (None [] 0))))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut nid) (+ (load nid) 1))
                (continue))))
    (set! (mut ci) 0)
    (loop (if (>= (load ci) (code-cfg-count))
              (break 0)
              (let [ret (code-cfg-at (load ci))]
                (if (= (ra-ideal-op ret) OP-RETURN)
                    (match (ra-enclosing-fun ret)
                      (Some [fun]
                            (let [owner (n-nid fun)
                                  max-location
                                    (match (get (load max-locations) owner)
                                      (Some [value] value)
                                      (None [] 0))]
                              (mach-finalize-active-frame fun
                                                          max-location
                                                          (hm-contains? (load call-functions) owner))
                              (set! (mut count) (+ (load count) 1))))
                      (None [] (panic "ra-finalize-frames!: Return has no enclosing Fun")))
                    0)
                (set! (mut ci) (+ (load ci) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load count)))

;; Bypass a same-block Split chain when an earlier source already occupies the desired output
;; register and no intervening instruction clobbers it. Final Simple performs this before deciding
;; whether the outer Split is a no-op; omitting it systematically preserves avoidable spill moves.
;; Its scheduled-result scan assumes clobbers are materialized as LRG definitions. Our AArch64
;; calls instead carry explicit kill masks, so the same no-clobber proof must consult both results
;; and those masks before bypassing a spill/reload pair across a call.
(defn ra-node-clobbers-reg? [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (reg i64)] (-> bool)
  (or (= (n-reg n) reg)
      (match (mach-of n)
        (Some [mach]
              (match (m-killmap mach)
                (Some [kills] (mask-test kills reg))
                (None [] false)))
        (None [] false))))

(defn ra-post-colour-bypass! [(split (dyn NodeOps)) (defreg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [block (ra-ifg-block-of split)
        split-index (ra-block-schedule-index block (n-nid split))
        (mut hi) (n-in! split 1)
        (mut found) false]
    (loop (if (or (load found)
                  (!= (n-op (load hi)) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                  (!= (n-block-nid (load hi)) (n-nid block))
                  (<= (n-nins (load hi)) 1))
              (break 0)
              (let [source (n-in! (load hi) 1)]
                (if (= (n-reg source) defreg)
                    (set! (mut found) true)
                    (set! (mut hi) source))
                (continue))))
    (if (or (not (load found)) (< split-index 0))
        false
        (let [(mut i) (- split-index 1)
              (mut clear) true]
          (loop (if (or (< (load i) 0) (not (load clear)))
                    (break 0)
                    (let [n (code-schedule-at block (load i))]
                      (if (n-same? n (load hi))
                          (break 0)
                          (if (ra-node-clobbers-reg? n defreg)
                              (set! (mut clear) false)
                              0))
                      (set! (mut i) (- (load i) 1))
                      (continue))))
          (if (and (load clear) (>= (load i) 0))
              (do
                (n-set-def! split 1 (Some (n-in! (load hi) 1)))
                true)
              false)))))

;; Remove no-op spills after attempting Simple's no-clobber chain bypass.
(defn ra-post-colour! [] (-> i64)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut remove) (al-new [i64] a)
        splits (ra-snapshot-scheduled-splits)]
    (ra-finalize-frames!)
    ;; Snapshot first: subsuming a split mutates the arena graph and may recursively collect its
    ;; input, so discovery and mutation must not share an output-list traversal.
    (let [(mut i) 0]
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (len splits))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (match (arena-node (get splits (load i)))
                    (Some [split]
                          (if (and (= (n-op split) OP-MACH-SPLIT) (> (n-nins split) 1))
                              (let [defreg (n-reg split)
                                    (mut usereg) (n-reg (n-in! split 1))]
                                (if (and (!= defreg (load usereg))
                                         (ra-post-colour-bypass! split defreg))
                                    (set! (mut usereg) (n-reg (n-in! split 1)))
                                    0)
                                (if (= defreg (load usereg))
                                    (push! [i64] (mut remove) (n-nid split))
                                    0))
                              0))
                    (None [] 0))
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    (let [(mut i) 0]
      (loop (if (>= (load i) (len (load remove)))
                (break 0)
                (do
                  (match (arena-node (get (load remove) (load i)))
                    (Some [split]
                          (if (and (not (n-dead? split))
                                   (= (n-op split) OP-MACH-SPLIT)
                                   (> (n-nins split) 1))
                              (n-subsume! split (n-in! split 1))
                              0))
                    (None [] 0))
                  (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                  (continue)))))
    (if (> (len (load remove)) 0) (code-schedule-compact!) 0)
    (len (load remove))))
